{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1543101-do-you-like-paradox","id":1543101,"title":"Do you like paradox?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Mage: The Ascension"],"posts":[{"date":"2024-10-04T08:00:37-07:00","id":1543101,"title":"Do you like paradox?","content":"Just curious, do you guys like the concept of paradox and the implications in game?<br /> <br /> I'm not asking about its mechanics per se, but the fluff. The role of paradox is to limit magick somehow, otherwise mages would fly around rebuilding reality as they please. So, do you think it's a good way to do that?<br /> or would you prefer another option like the famous &quot;mana&quot; points? Or DnD spells per day?<br /> <br /> If you could (or did) change how magick is limited in your game, how it would be?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3153-lord-revan","name":"Lord Revan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3153_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1419"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-10-04T09:10:09-07:00","id":1543103,"title":"","content":"Yup its fun. Makes magic dangerous.<br /> Personally i despise resource management.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28439-quelsec","name":"quelsec","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2024"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"407"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-10-04T13:29:57-07:00","id":1543118,"title":"","content":"Paradox isn't meant to limit magic in any way, shape or form. It not only doesn\u2019t keep Mages from flying around rebuilding reality as they please, it in fact messes things even more when it comes down.<br /> <br /> I think it fulfills its true purpose of reinforcing the theme of responsibility vs hubris. When Paradox happens, the Mage can blame lady luck as much as they want, they\u2019re actually the only one responsible for whatever consequence comes their way.<br /> <br /> Other than that, I think it must be toned to the kind of game you want. I repeat, it isn\u2019t really meant to limit anything. Even Revised-era Paradox does a crappy job at stopping Mages. Instead, it is there to make Magic dangerous, be it Gritty Survival mode (everything causes loads of Paradox), or just Flavored Failure (only big backlashes cause Paradox).<br /> <br /> What limits Mages in WoD is other Mages. Unless they\u2019re unnecessarily fearful without ever experiencing it, what players will really avoid is the response of something bigger and badder.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83e\udd70","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-10-05T07:06:59-07:00","id":1543144,"title":"","content":"I wouldn't mind replacing Paradox with Resonance. Or at least making Resonance central to Paradox. But as <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar5826_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"5826\" data-vbnamecard=\"5826\">monteparnas</a> points out, Paradox isn't so much about limiting mages as it is about ensuring that Magick has Consequences.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":421,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","user":"Dataweaver","date":". 10-05-2024, 10:11 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-10-05T09:51:52-07:00","id":1543150,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1543101-do-you-like-paradox?p=1543144#post1543144\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I wouldn't mind replacing Paradox with Resonance. Or at least making Resonance central to Paradox. But as <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar5826_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"5826\" data-vbnamecard=\"5826\">monteparnas</a> points out, Paradox isn't so much about limiting mages as it is about ensuring that Magick has Consequences.</div> </div> </div> </div>I definitely want to see more on Resonance but I don't think it should replace Paradox automatically. We need a Storyteller's Guide with a chapter on mixing an matching Paradox and Resonance to gain different story effects and moods.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/857-astromancer","name":"Astromancer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar857_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2195"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-10-05T16:05:08-07:00","id":1543167,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1543101-do-you-like-paradox?p=1543118#post1543118\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Paradox isn't meant to limit magic in any way, shape or form. It not only doesn\u2019t keep Mages from flying around rebuilding reality as they please, it in fact messes things even more when it comes down.</div> </div> </div> </div>I agree with that from an in-game perspective. But out of game, I feel paradox was kinda the way the authors found to explain why mages should avoid doing stuff in front of mortals. Vampires have the Masquerade, Garou have the Veil. While mages should be encouraged to use magick in front of sleepers, because that would help change concensus they way Trads wants.<br /> <br /> Of course, the Technocracy are a real menace too, but fighting them is inevitable and part of the game (for Trads).<br /> <br /> Also, giving something hard consequences is definitely a way of limitation. Kinda like the penal code?<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3153-lord-revan","name":"Lord Revan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3153_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1419"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-10-06T05:32:30-07:00","id":1543199,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Astromancer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1543101-do-you-like-paradox?p=1543150#post1543150\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I definitely want to see more on Resonance but I don't think it should replace Paradox automatically. We need a Storyteller's Guide with a chapter on mixing an matching Paradox and Resonance to gain different story effects and moods.</div> </div> </div> </div>I did a long time ago a few tables of &quot;Paradox Backlash&quot;, based on Paradigm, Sphere and Resonance. So, the idea was &quot;role 2 dice and check the table X for results&quot;. But I gave up on the idea for a more free style approach, but it's still doable.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28035-magus-maximus","name":"Magus Maximus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2023"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"569"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-10-06T05:34:03-07:00","id":1543200,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lord Revan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1543101-do-you-like-paradox?p=1543167#post1543167\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I agree with that from an in-game perspective. But out of game, I feel paradox was kinda the way the authors found to explain why mages should avoid doing stuff in front of mortals. Vampires have the Masquerade, Garou have the Veil. While mages should be encouraged to use magick in front of sleepers, because that would help change concensus they way Trads wants.<br /> <br /> Of course, the Technocracy are a real menace too, but fighting them is inevitable and part of the game (for Trads).<br /> <br /> Also, giving something hard consequences is definitely a way of limitation. Kinda like the penal code?</div> </div> </div> </div>It is obviously the meta-game way to do it, yes, even if it's not the in-game purpose. But I agree with both of you","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28035-magus-maximus","name":"Magus Maximus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2023"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"569"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-10-06T18:39:04-07:00","id":1543237,"title":"","content":"Even in a meta-game, Doylist perspective, I don\u2019t think Paradox was meant, or work, as a limitation. At most it encourages some thinking into trying to make the effect into a literal coincidence, but that\u2019s more of a style thing than a limitation on Magic on par with Mana or daily uses.<br /> <br /> Paradox doesn\u2019t make you think twice before casting. It makes you think on how to cast, which plays more on keeping you on the themes of the game than really placing any actual limitation on how often you use Magic, or how powerful the spell is.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-10-06T19:03:56-07:00","id":1543239,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1543101-do-you-like-paradox?p=1543237#post1543237\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Even in a meta-game, Doylist perspective, I don\u2019t think Paradox was meant, or work, as a limitation. At most it encourages some thinking into trying to make the effect into a literal coincidence, but that\u2019s more of a style thing than a limitation on Magic on par with Mana or daily uses.<br /> <br /> Paradox doesn\u2019t make you think twice before casting. It makes you think on how to cast, which plays more on keeping you on the themes of the game than really placing any actual limitation on how often you use Magic, or how powerful the spell is.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, of course it is a limitation. It is a severe punishment from vulgar effects. You might say &quot;well I never use vulgar effects&quot;, but deppending on the situation you might need to do it.<br /> <br /> Just compare how mages would behave with and without paradox and it's pretty clear how limiting it is<br /> <br /> I really dont get your point","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3153-lord-revan","name":"Lord Revan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3153_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1419"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-10-07T00:07:10-07:00","id":1543255,"title":"","content":"It's a consequence, not a limitation.<br /> <br /> It's also a consequence that, IMO, most players vastly overestimate. While editions vary here and there, the game effectively makes it so that you can easily eat 5-10 Paradox with minor consequences as long as you don't do it frequently. I remember one time my PC got 6 Paradox (Revised rules if it matters) in a fight and everyone thought I was nuts for taking such a big risk. 3 spent in a backlash at the end of the fight (soaked all the bashing damage, took a short term minor flaw), and the remaining 3 bleed off over three weeks of avoiding vulgar magic.<br /> <br /> And that's without a Familiar, Paradox magnet Wonder, or high level Prime to help.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83e\udd70","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-10-07T05:12:22-07:00","id":1543260,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1543101-do-you-like-paradox?p=1543255#post1543255\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It's a consequence, not a limitation.<br /> <br /> It's also a consequence that, IMO, most players vastly overestimate. While editions vary here and there, the game effectively makes it so that you can easily eat 5-10 Paradox with minor consequences as long as you don't do it frequently. I remember one time my PC got 6 Paradox (Revised rules if it matters) in a fight and everyone thought I was nuts for taking such a big risk. 3 spent in a backlash at the end of the fight (soaked all the bashing damage, took a short term minor flaw), and the remaining 3 bleed off over three weeks of avoiding vulgar magic.<br /> <br /> And that's without a Familiar, Paradox magnet Wonder, or high level Prime to help.</div> </div> </div> </div>I guys do realize that consequences impose limitations right? <br /> <br /> In your very example, you had to keep low profile for three weeks to bleed of the rest. If there wasnt paradox, your mage not only wouldn't get that (small) damage and flaw, but he could keep doing vulgar magick on a daily basis.<br /> <br /> The very consequence of paradox made him avoid vulgar magick.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3153-lord-revan","name":"Lord Revan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3153_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1419"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-10-07T05:51:02-07:00","id":1543262,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Magus Maximus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1543101-do-you-like-paradox?p=1543199#post1543199\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I did a long time ago a few tables of &quot;Paradox Backlash&quot;, based on Paradigm, Sphere and Resonance. So, the idea was &quot;role 2 dice and check the table X for results&quot;. But I gave up on the idea for a more free style approach, but it's still doable.</div> </div> </div> </div>I wouldn't do it through random tables. But at the very least, Resonance ought to flavor a mage's Paradox the way it does the Magick. <br /> <br /> But my initial point was that conceptually, I prefer the notion that Resonance has teeth; and that instead of tracking Paradox points to see when and if Backlashes are triggered, the whole system of magical consequences should be keyed off of how much Resonance you have. I have, for instance, taken to treating Quiet as one thing (instead of having the Madness/Denial/Morbidity divide), with the mage's Resonance flavoring it: Temperamental Resonance causes you to see things that aren't; Stabilizing Resonance causes to <i>not</i> see things that <i>are; </i>Elemental Resonance causes you to see the element infused in everything, exaggerating its influence; and Devotional Resonance causes the Quiet to reinforce your ethical beliefs and undercut anything that would contradict them. <br /> <br /> More generally though, I'd like a replacement for Paradox Backlashes that key off of the mage's Spheres: essentially, craft &quot;backlashes&quot; out of the mage's own Magick. You don't actually have &quot;Quiet&quot;; you have spontaneous Mind Effects. &quot;Paradox Spirits&quot; and &quot;Paradox Realms&quot; are manifestations of Spirit; and so on.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\u2615","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-10-07T08:40:37-07:00","id":1543265,"title":"","content":"I do like Paradox conceptually a lot. If not always it's particular mechanics<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lord Revan</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">I guys do realize that consequences impose limitations right?<br /> <br /> In your very example, you had to keep low profile for three weeks to bleed of the rest. If there wasnt paradox, your mage not only wouldn't get that (small) damage and flaw, but he could keep doing vulgar magick on a daily basis.<br /> <br /> The very consequence of paradox made him avoid vulgar magick.</div> </div> </div> </div>I can understand Paradox as a limitation of sorts. But it's not a limit in the sense of &quot;you can do X magick and not more&quot;. It's not so much a hard limit as a psychological one. It's more akin to a guts game.<br /> <br /> In D&amp;D you know exactly how much resources you can expend. There's tension in knowing that, by making this figth easier, you may not be able to face dangers afterwards. Once you've reached the limit, your magick goes away<br /> <br /> On Mage you can always push your luck harder. Because there's so much breadth in the RNG, the mage of the example could easily have chosen to keep firing Vulgar stuff, and not die. There's a level of &quot;resource management&quot; here, but to calculate the point where reciving hard consequences it's a given it's not just hard, but pointless, realisticly you're never going to survive until you reach the &quot;hard limit of Paradox&quot;. Ultimately the sampled player chosed to stop early and avoid the risks<br /> <br /> So, rather than &quot;resource management&quot;, there's more of a &quot;risk management&quot; going on <hr />I've been reading Dying Earth, and it's interesting how the author goes about his &quot;Vancian magick&quot;. The characters know the adversary has a limit, but there's tension in that they don't know *when* they're going to reach it. An adversary may seem impossibly powerful. But ultimately they know that exhaustion it's a viable strategy.<br /> <br /> On Mage that's not the same! , pushed against the ropes a mage will figth harder. Trying to &quot;invoke&quot; Paradox as a tactical limit it's not very feasible, and even if it does show up, you don't know if it's going to affect things to your advantage<br /> <br /> Interestingly, however, there's quite an amount of fiction on Mage that *does* show the figth ending when the mage *explodes* on Paradox. Meaning that the authors maybe thought of Paradox as a real tactical limit...And maybe that's why it's so common to hear about Paradox as that wich limits the power of mages, rather than a risk of practicing magick.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lord Revan</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">Of course, the Technocracy are a real menace too, but fighting them is inevitable and part of the game (for Trads).</div> </div> </div> </div>On Mage you're always the Underdog.<br /> <br /> If you're Tradition, you know that the Technocracy has you beaten, but also that it isn't taking it's full force against you rigth now. You can &quot;push it&quot;, but the more Vulgar you get, the more the Technocracy will prioritize you as a target, and at some point you're going to lose. So Mages try to figth subtly, as to make the &quot;risk/reward&quot; calculus of the Technocracy check them as &quot;not worth it&quot;<br /> <br /> If you're Technocracy, you have your superiors limiting what you can do in a similar fashion.<br /> <br /> Ultimately, it's all about &quot;consequences&quot;.<br /> <br /> But in practice the Technocracy it's the more certain consequence of going Vulgar, compared to Paradox. They're the reason to keep a Masquerade more than anything else (if you think about it, the Masquerade itself it's also a reacion to &quot;hunters&quot;, so it's not that different). <hr /><br /> Narratively, Paradox does act as a sort of obstacle of the more &quot;high end&quot; powers, and protects reality to some extent. Like how super old and powerful mages are keept in realms because they can't sustain their immortality on Earth. Or how super powerful rituals can end in catastrophic reasults. Or how Unbelief kicked Bygones out of reality, and whole places (like Lemuria) even. From the PoV of the Lore of Mage, Paradox and similar forces have been a stone in the foot of the true Fantastical, one could say.<br /> <br /> But players rarely experience any of this. For Players Paradox it's more of a reminder that magick it's inherently risky, a powerful but dangerous force that needs to be treated with caution. And that, perhaps more than the above, it's not something a standard &quot;Mana pool&quot; could easily replace<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1683,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","user":"Aleph","date":". 10-07-2024, 12:00 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","name":"Aleph","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3056"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-10-07T09:34:21-07:00","id":1543267,"title":"","content":"Paradox seems to have a few major applications and how much I approve of it depends on the application.<br /> <br /> The first is keeping magic unpredictable and risky, and I think the idea of paradox works well in this sense. The rules <br /> <br /> The second is highlighting the nature of magic and the consensus. This is most prominent in the role of witnesses and unbelief. Again, I think this functions reasonably well.<br /> <br /> The third is keeping the feel of earthly reality reasonably grounded. In this sense it works well for explaining why the major factions aren't waging a hot ascension war, but it doesn't do much to keep individual events from spiraling well out of control.<br /> <br /> The fourth is to punish specific things the authors or STs don't want to deal with. It's usually easy to tell because all the normal paradox rules go out the window and the points start flowing like someone cracked open a fire hydrant. Time travel is the most obvious version of this, but not the only one. I think this is the worst application of Paradox. It undercuts all the metaphysical and thematic elements and turns Paradox into a blunt punishing instrument.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Mage: The Ice-ension: An Epic Game of Reality on the Rink","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/758-ramnesis","name":"Ramnesis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar758_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2220"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-10-07T16:00:21-07:00","id":1543292,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lord Revan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1543101-do-you-like-paradox?p=1543260#post1543260\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I guys do realize that consequences impose limitations right?</div> </div> </div> </div>Not in the sense of the question proposed.<br /> <br /> Mana Points and Vancian tables are tools that recognize magic as a powerful option, and make it into a limited resource to compensate, so you can\u2019t solve all your problems with magic (and has to let your non-magical colleagues do their shit).<br /> <br /> Paradox is not a power limitator. It is a STYLE limitator. Since Coincidental magic isn\u2019t less powerful or significant than vulgar magic (just harder to think about), Paradox doesn\u2019t keep you from abusing magic, weak or strong, doesn\u2019t keep you from solving every single problem with magic if you want, and doesn\u2019t balance the Mage against any \u2018non-spellcaster\u2019.<br /> <br /> What it does is to justify the setting. It justifies characters full of Permadox being secluded. It justifies (in a tangential way) fantastic things in general being locked in secluded spaces or in other worlds. And it justifies and reinforces Mages taking preference for being subtle with their Magic.<br /> <br /> That\u2019s a very distinct form of limitation than what is tackled by points or slots of magic. It simply doesn\u2019t serve the same purpose, in any way whatsoever, and that was your original proposition.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83e\udd70","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-10-07T17:24:02-07:00","id":1543301,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar1683_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"1683\" data-vbnamecard=\"1683\">Aleph</a> , very well put. I agree with practically everything and now I understand what you mean by &quot;it's not a limitation&quot;. Actually, as <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar5826_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"5826\" data-vbnamecard=\"5826\">monteparnas</a> , it is a different kind of limitation. One where you can keeps casting whenever you want regardless of &quot;points&quot;.<br /> <br /> I just have some observations:<br /> <br /> - The Technocracy is as strong as the ST wants it to be, so it *might* be a limitng factor or not so muuch<br /> <br /> - Unlike the Masquerade or Veil, it isn't considered a &quot;crime&quot; by his peers for mages to cast vulgar spells, quite the contrary, it is &quot;encouraged&quot; as a way to change consensus<br /> <br /> - There could be a system of points/mana that isn't limited daily. For example, the mage could regain points by minutes/hours, or in some other ways, like meditating or something to restore points. Tbh, D&amp;D is quire like that, since casters can rest and restore their spells (of course, some DMs might limit resting).<br /> <br /> So, do you think there is a better system of keeping magick on track? Have this ever been tought about by you guys?<br /> <br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/758-ramnesis\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar758_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"758\" data-vbnamecard=\"758\">Ramnesis</a> , I share some of your opinons. I'm not sure magick should be unpredictable or risky, just hard and maybe exhausting. And one thing I don't like at all is the unbelief rule, especially because there isnt one and it's just too vague...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3153-lord-revan","name":"Lord Revan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3153_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1419"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-10-08T06:58:29-07:00","id":1543335,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lord Revan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1543101-do-you-like-paradox?p=1543301#post1543301\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/758-ramnesis\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar758_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"758\" data-vbnamecard=\"758\">Ramnesis</a> , I share some of your opinons. I'm not sure magick should be unpredictable or risky, just hard and maybe exhausting. And one thing I don't like at all is the unbelief rule, especially because there isnt one and it's just too vague...</div> </div> </div> </div>As an element of a fantasy world, I don't think magic has to be unpredictable, risky, hard, or have any other limitation. As a dramatic element, and especially as a dramatic element for a game, it probably should have some kind of challenge or barrier to overcome. And if there has to be a challenge, it is best if it fits the nature of the world or the themes of the story. For Mage, I would choose unpredictable and hard over exhausting. The former two speak to the nature of Mage's metaphysics, while the latter one doesn't.<br /> <br /> As for unbelief, I agree. I'm surprised there isn't at least some kind of structure. In another game I'd suggest that there was no need to define something that could be left up to the story, but Mage defines things unnecessarily all the time. Unbelief is something I actually prefer to handle narratively, though, so I'm not complaining.<br /> <br /> I suspect that the issue is that rules would cause some consequences the authors don't want to deal with. After all, Unbelief is not limited to awakened magic, it hits other things too (Bygones are a prominent example). If anything that sleepers disbelieved strongly enough would end in X scenes, there would be a few changes to the world.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Mage: The Ice-ension: An Epic Game of Reality on the Rink","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/758-ramnesis","name":"Ramnesis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar758_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2220"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-10-08T08:40:08-07:00","id":1543340,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lord Revan</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">So, do you think there is a better system of keeping magick on track? Have this ever been tought about by you guys?</div> </div> </div> </div>&quot;on track&quot; depends on<i> what tracks</i> you want magick to be.<br /> <br /> There are games that have systems of magick that, <i>for the purposes of those games</i> (themes, narrative, gameplay experience), I think work better than what Paradox does for Mage. But those systems wouldn't do if ported to Mage w/o some heavy changes.<br /> <br /> For the purposes of Mage, I do like magick being risky, and I do like how Paradox encourages mages to think about how to pass what they do as &quot;luck&quot;. But Paradox rules can be a bit cumbersome and nonsensical sometimes. Vague to non-existent other times.<br /> <br /> *The &quot;new&quot; True Black Hand book for Vampire has a system of Paradox that was much simpler. Something like turning Paradox successes into successes for a &quot;spell&quot; - it's simple as simple goes, and allows the ST to have a lot of control of how Paradox manifests. It just covers backlashes, tho. <br /> <br /> *As many have said, rules to incorporate Ressonance into it would be pretty good. If Paradox it's &quot;consequences&quot;, it is thematic that the consequence actually get's flavored by how you use your magick<br /> <br /> *As <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar5826_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"5826\" data-vbnamecard=\"5826\">monteparnas</a> exelently puts it, Paradox it's a &quot;style limitator&quot; . That beeing the case, and being allowed to dream, I think it could be cool if that didn't just reduced to trying to be subtle.<br /> <br /> &quot;Consequences&quot; don't need to <i>always </i>be bad. It could be interesting that there was a third option to handle Paradox to the two options of &quot;being subtle to avoid it&quot; and &quot;building your mage to tank it&quot;, adding something aking to &quot;riding Paradox&quot;: An option to have the consequences of using magick go rougly your way, even if not under your control and ultimately dangerous.<br /> <br /> Perhaps even creating a dichotomy similar to how Changeling handles the Dreaming as a source of power and shield against Banality, but that can also loose your character to it's madness if you don't ever return to reality ...&quot;loosing yourself to magick&quot; IT'S something that can happen in Mage (Marauders), but it's never a choice, a risk you can take as a player, nor a style you can really play to","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1683,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","user":"Aleph","date":". 10-08-2024, 11:48 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83e\udd70","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","name":"Aleph","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3056"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-10-08T09:56:25-07:00","id":1543345,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ramnesis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1543101-do-you-like-paradox?p=1543335#post1543335\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> As an element of a fantasy world, I don't think magic has to be unpredictable, risky, hard, or have any other limitation. As a dramatic element, and especially as a dramatic element for a game, it probably should have some kind of challenge or barrier to overcome. And if there has to be a challenge, it is best if it fits the nature of the world or the themes of the story. For Mage, I would choose unpredictable and hard over exhausting. The former two speak to the nature of Mage's metaphysics, while the latter one doesn't.<br /> <br /> As for unbelief, I agree. I'm surprised there isn't at least some kind of structure. In another game I'd suggest that there was no need to define something that could be left up to the story, but Mage defines things unnecessarily all the time. Unbelief is something I actually prefer to handle narratively, though, so I'm not complaining.<br /> <br /> I suspect that the issue is that rules would cause some consequences the authors don't want to deal with. After all, Unbelief is not limited to awakened magic, it hits other things too (Bygones are a prominent example). If anything that sleepers disbelieved strongly enough would end in X scenes, there would be a few changes to the world.</div> </div> </div> </div>My view on this is that Bygones are creatures of Magick, in much the same way that <b>Changeling</b>'s chimera are fae. I don't know what exactly that <i>means, </i>because <b>Mage</b> makes a point <i>not</i> to nail down exactly what Magick is; but <i>whatever</i> it is, Bygones are tapped into it. And <i>because</i> they're tapped into it, they're vulnerable to Unbelief.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-10-08T10:35:03-07:00","id":1543348,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aleph</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1543101-do-you-like-paradox?p=1543340#post1543340\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">*The &quot;new&quot; True Black Hand book for Vampire has a system of Paradox that was much simpler. Something like turning Paradox successes into successes for a &quot;spell&quot; - it's simple as simple goes, and allows the ST to have a lot of control of how Paradox manifests. It just covers backlashes, tho.</div> </div> </div> </div>I was intending to mention this. It's what I was thinking about when I said &quot;More generally though, I'd like a replacement for Paradox Backlashes that key off of the mage's Spheres: essentially, craft 'backlashes' out of the mage's own Magick. You don't actually have 'Quiet'; you have spontaneous Mind Effects. 'Paradox Spirits' and 'Paradox Realms' are manifestations of Spirit; and so on.&quot;<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aleph</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1543101-do-you-like-paradox?p=1543340#post1543340\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">*As many have said, rules to incorporate Ressonance into it would be pretty good. If Paradox it's &quot;consequences&quot;, it is thematic that the consequence actually get's flavored by how you use your magick<br /> <br /> *As <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar5826_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"5826\" data-vbnamecard=\"5826\">monteparnas</a> exelently puts it, Paradox it's a &quot;style limitator&quot; . That beeing the case, and being allowed to dream, I think it could be cool if that didn't just reduced to trying to be subtle.<br /> <br /> &quot;Consequences&quot; don't need to <i>always </i>be bad. It could be interesting that there was a third option to handle Paradox to the two options of &quot;being subtle to avoid it&quot; and &quot;building your mage to tank it&quot;, adding something aking to &quot;riding Paradox&quot;: An option to have the consequences of using magick go rougly your way, even if not under your control and ultimately dangerous.</div> </div> </div> </div>A bit like C20's Unleashings. That said, <b>Mage</b> has Wild Magick, which is completely and totally under the Storyteller's control; even in terms of when it happens. As described, it only seems to happen in two cases: when you first Awaken, or when you're a Marauder. <br /> <br /> Deliberate Wild Magick strikes me as something that could be suitable to a number of different Practices: one might unleash a burst of Wild Magick through Faith, for example, by saying a prayer and asking the higher power that you serve to intervene however it deems best; or a practitioner of Chaos Magick could borrow a line from <i>The Last Unicorn</i>: &quot;Magick, do as you will&quot;. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aleph</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1543101-do-you-like-paradox?p=1543340#post1543340\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Perhaps even creating a dichotomy similar to how Changeling handles the Dreaming as a source of power and shield against Banality, but that can also loose your character to it's madness if you don't ever return to reality ...&quot;loosing yourself to magick&quot; IT'S something that can happen in Mage (Marauders), but it's never a choice, a risk you can take as a player, nor a style you can really play to</div> </div> </div> </div>I'd consider tying &quot;Wild&quot; Magick to the Avatar: say that what it actually is is your Avatar working Magick on its own. So the higher your Avatar Background, the more potent and/or frequent Wild Magick becomes. I'm not sure exactly what mechanics I'd use; but one possibility would be to substitute your Avatar rating for Sphere requirements of an Wild Effect.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-10-08T10:55:08-07:00","id":1543350,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1543101-do-you-like-paradox?p=1543345#post1543345\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> My view on this is that Bygones are creatures of Magick, in much the same way that <b>Changeling</b>'s chimera are fae. I don't know what exactly that <i>means, </i>because <b>Mage</b> makes a point <i>not</i> to nail down exactly what Magick is; but <i>whatever</i> it is, Bygones are tapped into it. And <i>because</i> they're tapped into it, they're vulnerable to Unbelief.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's certainly one way of dealing with it, and it would answer the question of why the Unicorn was pushed out of reality but the Giraffe was not. On the flip side, some Bygones aren't particularly supernatural, certainly no more so than the aforementioned leopard-moose-camel with the 7 foot neck (to use the meme). It's hard to see any reason why we would tie them to awakened magic other than that they disappeared<br /> <br /> Not that I have an answer to why some creatures are bygones and others are not, but I still lean towards unbelief affecting a wider swath of things than just awakened magic. There seems to be a need to explain why vampires and werewolves are not affected by unbelief, after all, which tells me that by all rights it should.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Mage: The Ice-ension: An Epic Game of Reality on the Rink","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/758-ramnesis","name":"Ramnesis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar758_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2220"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-10-08T14:26:44-07:00","id":1543359,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lord Revan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1543101-do-you-like-paradox?p=1543301#post1543301\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">[USER=&quot;1683&quot;]<br /> - The Technocracy is as strong as the ST wants it to be, so it *might* be a limitng factor or not so muuch</div> </div> </div> </div>Setting aside players that fear Paradox far more than it is warranted by the rules given, They\u2019re the bigger concern between the two regardless, as they\u2019re the literal Game Police that will come to get you if you play it wrong.<br /> <br /> And Paradox itself is also as strong as the ST wants it to be. Between DA, SC, Classic and Revised Mage already had 4 distinct levels/flavor of Paradox at \u201cplayable\u201d ages, plus two lesser levels that only existed on fluf for now: \u201cPermadox\u201d making Magic harder instead of dangerous, and no Paradox at all, as the whole thing only existed since about the turn of the 10th to 11th centuries.<br /> <br /> The point is, Mage doesn\u2019t need Paradox. It doesn\u2019t need any limitation to Magic at all. The game was designed for Magic and it works with Magic being cast non-stop. What keeps the setting glued together, as far as it goes, is the presence of Mages that do so on purpose, be them the Union or others.<br /> <br /> If you prefer to explore themes of magic being hard and tiresome, go for it. The basics of the game don\u2019t change much. Maybe \u201cParadox\u201d is a measure of tiredness, instead of being played as a dicepool it keeps you from casting once reaching a certain point (Stamina comes to mind, but I\u2019d avoid linking it to a given trait as it affects character builds. Maybe to Arete?).<br /> <br /> Just relax about the idea that the game needs mechanical limitations on Magic. It doesn\u2019t, really. Paradox is, at the end, just an attached system that doesn\u2019t affect any other directly, so it can be exchanged or eliminated with ease.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1543101-do-you-like-paradox?p=1543348#post1543348\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I was intending to mention this. It's what I was thinking about when I said &quot;More generally though, I'd like a replacement for Paradox Backlashes that key off of the mage's Spheres: essentially, craft 'backlashes' out of the mage's own Magick. You don't actually have 'Quiet'; you have spontaneous Mind Effects. 'Paradox Spirits' and 'Paradox Realms' are manifestations of Spirit; and so on.&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>I think this can be done with the systems we have. The Paradox roll could work as an Arete roll, and the ST builds an effect from the Mage\u2019s Spheres and Resonance.<br /> <br /> For Paradox Realms, I think the harder part is to actually devise the realms. A list of examples is much needed.<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1543101-do-you-like-paradox?p=1543348#post1543348\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I'd consider tying &quot;Wild&quot; Magick to the Avatar: say that what it actually is is your Avatar working Magick on its own. So the higher your Avatar Background, the more potent and/or frequent Wild Magick becomes. I'm not sure exactly what mechanics I'd use; but one possibility would be to substitute your Avatar rating for Sphere requirements of an Wild Effect.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'd tie Wild Magic to reduced difficulty. It could be equivalent to using one or two Instruments, so you cast at a low dif with little preparation, but you give up control over the precise effect. For loosing control, I\u2019d keep the Unleashing rules, you screw it if you get more successes than your Sphere rating.<br /> <br /> This could be just loss of control, or the excess successes could become Paradox.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ramnesis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1543101-do-you-like-paradox?p=1543350#post1543350\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> On the flip side, some Bygones aren't particularly supernatural, certainly no more so than the aforementioned leopard-moose-camel with the 7 foot neck (to use the meme). It's hard to see any reason why we would tie them to awakened magic other than that they disappeared<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>It could be that they were originally created by Magic or a somewhat similar power. In that scenario, what defines a bygone is its true history, even if this history isn\u2019t known to the Mage. The creature having preternatural powers is then irrelevant to their status as a bygone.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-10-09T02:41:33-07:00","id":1543406,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1543101-do-you-like-paradox?p=1543348#post1543348\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">A bit like C20's Unleashings. That said, <b>Mage</b> has Wild Magick, which is completely and totally under the Storyteller's control; even in terms of when it happens. As described, it only seems to happen in two cases: when you first Awaken, or when you're a Marauder.<br /> <br /> Deliberate Wild Magick strikes me as something that could be suitable to a number of different Practices: one might unleash a burst of Wild Magick through Faith, for example, by saying a prayer and asking the higher power that you serve to intervene however it deems best; or a practitioner of Chaos Magick could borrow a line from <i>The Last Unicorn</i>: &quot;Magick, do as you will&quot;.</div> </div> </div> </div>Okay, now I kind of want to include a Houserule for Mage called &quot;Magick, Do As You Will&quot;. Wherein at any time, or perhaps just in dramatically appropriate moments, the PC can trigger Wild Magick. But importantly, it's &quot;<i>Magick</i>, Do As You Will&quot;. The Mage herself has no control over the Effect, its potency, how it behaves, or who gets targeted. The PC is effectively using herself as a conduit for the primal forces of Magick to act, in whatever way these mysterious forces want.<br /> <br /> Ex: The Cabal are in a tight spot in an art gallery, and either can't or won't use their own Spheres to solve the problem. So one PC says &quot;fuck it. Magick, Do As You Will&quot;. Suddenly, all the paintings and statues come to life. Has it made the situation better or worse? The PC certainly had no input in it, but they can still respond to the change in whatever way they see fit.<br /> <br /> It's a sort of risky ploy, channeling raw Magick into an environment normally bound by a rigid Consensus. Like they've opened a crack in the shell of calcified Reality, and let the power of primordial creation and dreams leak in.<br /> <br /> (Naturally, Paradox does NOT like Mages doing this.)<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I'd consider tying &quot;Wild&quot; Magick to the Avatar: say that what it actually is is your Avatar working Magick on its own. So the higher your Avatar Background, the more potent and/or frequent Wild Magick becomes. I'm not sure exactly what mechanics I'd use; but one possibility would be to substitute your Avatar rating for Sphere requirements of an Wild Effect. </div> </div> </div>This can act as yet another dramatic release valve. Avatars, by their nature, want their Mage proteges to advance. Not necessarily LIVE, mind you, because they can always reincarnate. But the Avatar is, at least nominally, concerned with the Mage. So if the Storyteller decides a situation is getting dire, they can have the player roll their Avatar rating instead of Arete.<br /> <br /> This may involve the Avatar appearing, to everyone or just the Mage, to render assistance. Or simply to goad the PC into continuing to struggle, or do whatever else the Avatar wants. Maybe the Avatar gives advice, or offers to guide the Mage's hand (possibly letting them use a Sphere or Sphere level they don't have, as a kind of taste of what power they COULD wield). Or the Avatar may act on their own, manifesting some Effect as appropriate to their apparent nature or interests.<br /> <br /> Ex: A PC's Avatar normally appears to them as a shadowy Roc that blots out the sun. In her time of need, the Mage's Avatar seemingly appears before everyone present. The ceiling, if any, falls away, revealing a sky that's then immediately blotted out by a terrible bird with titanic wings. It's an illusion, yes, but it strikes fear into the heart of every character present, as a being of a scale beyond mortal comprehension makes itself known.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://archiveofourown.org/works/6956863/chapters/15862327\" target=\"_blank\">Magestuck: The Ascension</a></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6156-bluecho","name":"Bluecho","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6156_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3871"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-10-09T07:03:20-07:00","id":1543421,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1543101-do-you-like-paradox?p=1543359#post1543359\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> It could be that they were originally created by Magic or a somewhat similar power. In that scenario, what defines a bygone is its true history, even if this history isn\u2019t known to the Mage. The creature having preternatural powers is then irrelevant to their status as a bygone.</div> </div> </div> </div>That leads to three possibilities that I can think of:<br /> <br /> 1) Bygones, regardless of their lore, are the creations of mages. This works well on a case by case basis but it doesn't work as a broad explanation for bygones. That is, it reduces all the myths and legends to misunderstandings of the acts of mages.<br /> <br /> 2) There is an arbitrary set of things that use awakened magic rather than anything else, and every bygone is one of these or the creation of one of these. This is workable, but it doesn't really tell us anything about the world. If the goal is to say that unbelief only works on awakened magic, this accomplishes that, but circularly.<br /> <br /> 3) Bygones have their own origins in culture or lore or history, but this still counts as awakened magic. This is the other end of the spectrum, where unbelief can strike almost anything. It is functionally the same thing as saying unbelief can affect things other than awakened magic, just accomplished by opening up awakened magic to mean almost anything.<br /> <br /> The third option suits me just fine as I don't tend to draw much distinction between the effects of the Consensus and the effects of intentional magic, but I think it is simpler to just say that Unbelief has the same vast powers as belief, just applied negatively.<br /> <br /> Because unbelief is so open ended it is hard to pin down its limits, so attempts to define it purely in terms of awakened magic will always struggle to avoid the circular reasoning trap: What does unbelief work on? Awakened magic. What is awakened magic? Whatever unbelief works on.<br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Mage: The Ice-ension: An Epic Game of Reality on the Rink","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/758-ramnesis","name":"Ramnesis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar758_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2220"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-10-09T10:16:57-07:00","id":1543430,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aleph</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1543101-do-you-like-paradox?p=1543340#post1543340\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> *As many have said, rules to incorporate Ressonance into it would be pretty good. If Paradox it's &quot;consequences&quot;, it is thematic that the consequence actually get's flavored by how you use your magick<br /> <br /> *As <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar5826_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"5826\" data-vbnamecard=\"5826\">monteparnas</a> exelently puts it, Paradox it's a &quot;style limitator&quot; . That beeing the case, and being allowed to dream, I think it could be cool if that didn't just reduced to trying to be subtle.<br /> <br /> &quot;Consequences&quot; don't need to <i>always </i>be bad. It could be interesting that there was a third option to handle Paradox to the two options of &quot;being subtle to avoid it&quot; and &quot;building your mage to tank it&quot;, adding something aking to &quot;riding Paradox&quot;: An option to have the consequences of using magick go rougly your way, even if not under your control and ultimately dangerous.<br /> <br /> Perhaps even creating a dichotomy similar to how Changeling handles the Dreaming as a source of power and shield against Banality, but that can also loose your character to it's madness if you don't ever return to reality ...&quot;loosing yourself to magick&quot; IT'S something that can happen in Mage (Marauders), but it's never a choice, a risk you can take as a player, nor a style you can really play to</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, wild magick or &quot;riding Paradox&quot; doesn't change much how the limitation works, both in and out of game. I mean, why reality *have* to fight against magick, and most importantly why it have to fight this way (with more magick)?<br /> <br /> I share your feeling completely, in Mage, we have these two options of &quot;going subtle&quot; or &quot;building to tank dox&quot;. To be honest, I believe most people try to merge both, going subtle when possible and, if you plan to go vulgar at least get a familiar or something, an if you keep going vulgar eventually you will get a bad time with dox...<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1543101-do-you-like-paradox?p=1543359#post1543359\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Setting aside players that fear Paradox far more than it is warranted by the rules given, They\u2019re the bigger concern between the two regardless, as they\u2019re the literal Game Police that will come to get you if you play it wrong.<br /> <br /> And Paradox itself is also as strong as the ST wants it to be. Between DA, SC, Classic and Revised Mage already had 4 distinct levels/flavor of Paradox at \u201cplayable\u201d ages, plus two lesser levels that only existed on fluf for now: \u201cPermadox\u201d making Magic harder instead of dangerous, and no Paradox at all, as the whole thing only existed since about the turn of the 10th to 11th centuries.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, paradox have hard rules, points, etc. So it is not completely up to the ST (we are discussing raw here, of course HR can change that). The Technocracy *is* completely controlled by the ST.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1543101-do-you-like-paradox?p=1543359#post1543359\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The point is, Mage doesn\u2019t need Paradox. It doesn\u2019t need any limitation to Magic at all. The game was designed for Magic and it works with Magic being cast non-stop. What keeps the setting glued together, as far as it goes, is the presence of Mages that do so on purpose, be them the Union or others.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, as long as you keep coincident. I understand your point, you could use magick non-stop because it doesn't need any resource other than rolling Arete (most of them), but you also cant cast non-stop with vulgar magick or you will quickly blow up (or worse).<br /> <br /> While sometimes going coincident is cool, I feel it kinda takes away the soul of the game if done constantly.[/quote]<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1543101-do-you-like-paradox?p=1543359#post1543359\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If you prefer to explore themes of magic being hard and tiresome, go for it. The basics of the game don\u2019t change much. Maybe \u201cParadox\u201d is a measure of tiredness, instead of being played as a dicepool it keeps you from casting once reaching a certain point (Stamina comes to mind, but I\u2019d avoid linking it to a given trait as it affects character builds. Maybe to Arete?).</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, I am just wondering about it. The working in-game should change, though. I mean, reality wouldn't &quot;fight back&quot;.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1543101-do-you-like-paradox?p=1543359#post1543359\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Just relax about the idea that the game needs mechanical limitations on Magic. It doesn\u2019t, really. Paradox is, at the end, just an attached system that doesn\u2019t affect any other directly, so it can be exchanged or eliminated with ease.</div> </div> </div> </div>Hm..I never imagined the game without paradox at all. I think you are right, it might be doable. A ST would probably have to find a way of controling the players abuse, and the only thing left for that would be the technocracy.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3153-lord-revan","name":"Lord Revan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3153_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1419"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-10-09T10:27:46-07:00","id":1543431,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ramnesis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1543101-do-you-like-paradox?p=1543421#post1543421\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> That leads to three possibilities that I can think of:<br /> <br /> 1) Bygones, regardless of their lore, are the creations of mages. This works well on a case by case basis but it doesn't work as a broad explanation for bygones. That is, it reduces all the myths and legends to misunderstandings of the acts of mages.<br /> <br /> 2) There is an arbitrary set of things that use awakened magic rather than anything else, and every bygone is one of these or the creation of one of these. This is workable, but it doesn't really tell us anything about the world. If the goal is to say that unbelief only works on awakened magic, this accomplishes that, but circularly.<br /> <br /> 3) Bygones have their own origins in culture or lore or history, but this still counts as awakened magic. This is the other end of the spectrum, where unbelief can strike almost anything. It is functionally the same thing as saying unbelief can affect things other than awakened magic, just accomplished by opening up awakened magic to mean almost anything.<br /> <br /> The third option suits me just fine as I don't tend to draw much distinction between the effects of the Consensus and the effects of intentional magic, but I think it is simpler to just say that Unbelief has the same vast powers as belief, just applied negatively.<br /> <br /> Because unbelief is so open ended it is hard to pin down its limits, so attempts to define it purely in terms of awakened magic will always struggle to avoid the circular reasoning trap: What does unbelief work on? Awakened magic. What is awakened magic? Whatever unbelief works on.<br /> <br /></div> </div> </div> </div>Unbelief is directly tied to Consensus, so I guess what makes a creature bygone is the Consensus. I heard an excuse about why Vampires and Werewolves can exist on earth, something related how they &quot;pay&quot; the price of Quintessence with Vitae and Gnose, or something like that...<br /> <br /> Anyway, I find Unbelief a crappy rule that only has lore application and shouldn't be used in a game. I think it's kinda the authors tool provided to ST to deal with players going crazy on their effects, although dox and crats should be enough for that, so I really don't see the point of it...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3153-lord-revan","name":"Lord Revan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3153_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1419"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-10-09T13:35:29-07:00","id":1543439,"title":"","content":"Paradox is a nice way to keep it an urban semi-horror instead of fantasy whatevery. If mages did not have to hide their magic this would not be world of darkness.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28439-quelsec","name":"quelsec","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2024"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"407"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-10-09T13:52:24-07:00","id":1543442,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ramnesis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1543101-do-you-like-paradox?p=1543421#post1543421\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> The third option suits me just fine as I don't tend to draw much distinction between the effects of the Consensus and the effects of intentional magic, but I think it is simpler to just say that Unbelief has the same vast powers as belief, just applied negatively.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>I think both the second and third options are workable. The second option is at first a circular explanation, but it is useful in the sense that you can actually define what those Magic-using things are for a given chronicle.<br /> <br /> Do godheads, all or some of them, do that? Do some classes of spirits, like the Djinn? Maybe Angels and/or Demons? Are there particular circumstances that empower normal humans to make their beliefs into acts of Magic?<br /> <br /> My point here is, this explanation is a good option for chronicles where you want to actively explore the origins of some bygones, or some power that can create them.<br /> <br /> The third option, where Bygones are a creation of Consensus to begin with, works just fine, but then we have things that are arbitrarily not a creation from the Consensus, and so not affected by Unbelief. In my opinion, it is actually just a mirror of the second, it\u2019s most relevant when the chronicle involves exploring the origins of a non-bygone supernatural entity.<br /> <br /> Other than that, they also affect how much the Consensus is a proven fact in your game, which may make one or the other a necessary answer. I don\u2019t think the first option is good, either.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lord Revan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1543101-do-you-like-paradox?p=1543430#post1543430\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Well, paradox have hard rules, points, etc. So it is not completely up to the ST (we are discussing raw here, of course HR can change that). The Technocracy *is* completely controlled by the ST.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, but it actually has 4 different sets of hard rules to choose from. Of course, they\u2019re meant as historical changes, but since M20 they reverted to 2nd ed levels and the book itself makes it optional which set to use.<br /> <br /> There\u2019s no canon on how strong Paradox is after 2004, it\u2019s up in the air.<br /> <br /> As I said, the game doesn\u2019t need Paradox to begin with, it\u2019s just a thematic mechanic. You can change, exchange or just drop it. Don\u2019t worry about the players abusing Magic, that\u2019s actually the intent of the game: they will abuse, and they will deal with whatever consequences you want to put on their path.<br /> <br /> Put whatever consequences are fun for you.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-10-13T17:42:59-07:00","id":1543717,"title":"","content":"I have become less convinced of the value of Paradox as an object in the setting over the years. I think that Paradox is best for emulating the trope of magicians tampering with great powers, or with struggling to perform great works of magic without something going awry. Of course, it is also quite obvious that Paradox was intended to be the masquerade-enforcer of the setting, and that is something that I do not really think is needed. The transformation of the Scourge to Paradox renders it quite clear that the focus of the latter is to force mages to use coincidental magic for the most part, and that is honestly something that seems more up the alley of sorcerers than mages.<br /> <br /> More broadly, I just have a problem with with the thought processes behind employing masquerade-enforcers in one's setting in general. I think that people seem to assume that a few careless mages firing off a few vulgar spells is enough to clue in the entire world to the presence of Awakened magic, when such is not the case. First off, all but the most far-reaching vulgar spells would probably only be witnessed by a few Sleepers, and the testimony of a few witnesses is generally not enough to convince the average person that a supernatural event has occurred, let alone the populace. Second, this situation is already present in the base setting, as once a mage is able to actually perform a vulgar spell, the Sleeper just knows about it, the consequences of Paradox be damned. Paradox just discourages mages from casting vulgar spells; it does not prevent the consequences of vulgar spells to continue affecting reality. In general, supernatural phenomena need to have three main elements in order to be accepted by a society. They need to be strong, they need to be relatively frequent, and they need to be relatively accessible. Awakened magic fails in regard to the latter two points, as mages are not obligated to cast vulgar spells incessantly and not everyone has unfettered access to Awakened magic. You do not need to have a mechanical system limiting magic to justify why the supernatural is not generally accepted by society. We already live in a world where universities publish the results of experiments with psychic phenomena, people can see strange objects in the sky, and people talk with spirits. I think that people often think that a limiting mechanism is required in the cosmology of the setting for a masquerade to be understandable, but really, there are a lot of ways for mundane social factors to just prevent the acceptance of the supernatural by the public.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28352-verlan","name":"Verlan","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2024"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"118"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-10-14T20:12:12-07:00","id":1543819,"title":"","content":"I heart Paradox; it gives consequences to the player-mages actions. This a check and balance and it keeps the game interesting; as a ST, it keeps me on my toes thinking of new, creative-ways it can effect the players and the game.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;I have all the power in the world to give you, and all you have to do is beg&quot; -Nix<br /> <br /> &quot;There's thing about being a vampire, Frank; it takes a long fucking time to learn how do all the cool shit&quot;. -Abigail","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2521-iguazu","name":"Iguazu","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2521_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"740"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-10-15T09:56:45-07:00","id":1543880,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lord Revan</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">Well, wild magick or &quot;riding Paradox&quot; doesn't change much how the limitation works, both in and out of game...</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Trully <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar421_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"421\" data-vbnamecard=\"421\">Dataweaver</a> ideas on Wild Magick don't directly touch Paradox, but I think they could function as the basis for some system that <i>does touch </i>it<br /> <br /> *I like &quot;Invoking Wild Magick&quot; use of Avatar as Spheres (if only because it gives more meat to having higher Avatar than 3) - also it's cool because in the Lore Awakenings with powerful Wild Magick are usually an indication of the mage having a strong Avatar.<br /> <br /> But what defines the potency of the effect?. Rolling Arete it's the normal way, I think Avatar could work as a replacement in this case (after all, recent Awakened don't have strong Arete).<br /> <br /> What about if we <i>add </i>Paradox to it?. That way there could be an incentive to actually have some dots on your wheel, in spite of the risks, because it could allow one to have a lot of &quot;instant&quot; power (that unprepared mages normally lack).<br /> <br /> Although it's not a power that you can control very well, I do think that at least there should be some way to determine some degree of general Intent. Otherwise nobody it's going to use it, considering it's risks. The wizard on the &quot;Last Unicorn&quot; couldn't know what magic would do, but he really trusted magic wasn't going to do something useless or anticlimactic, like dropping an anvil on the unicorn, or NOT doing anything at all to <i>protect </i>her, or the movie would have ended on a &quot;Magic, WTF!?&quot; <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> , note ... and that wasn't the idea<br /> <br /> I would take the mage's intent. Then use Ressonance, Avatar's Essence, and the Avatar's own goals and relationship to the mage, as things that could deviate from it (or the &quot;Will&quot; of Magick, as it may be). <hr /><br /> *With &quot;ridding Paradox&quot; I was thinking along the lines of Vampire &quot;ridding the Beast&quot;. A way to have some degree of control in exchange for a different risk.<br /> <br /> As an idea Taking the &quot;Black Hand&quot; as basis:<br /> <br /> On a backlash, there could be a mechanic (perhaps tied to your Arete or Avatar rating) to suggest one or more &quot;aspects&quot; of the resultant spell. An &quot;aspect&quot; could be something from the magickal effects tables, such as Damage, Duration or Targets, could also be things like removing one Sphere from the Effect, or determining which Ressonance it's going to be used to colour the backlash (providing that these do matter, and that you have more than one)<br /> I.E: you could determine that Paradox isn't going to cause damage directly. Or you could declare more than one targets + no Correspondence, and suddenly your Paradox becomes a potential problem for everyone arround you<br /> <br /> Perhaps this could be restricted to (or facilitated by) some kind of Focus. Like how Dataweaver suggests &quot;Wild Magick&quot; for Faith based Focuses, it could be the special thing for a fourth category of Focus:<br /> <br /> I'm thinking about some Akashicks and Extatics here. These are typically regarded as &quot;mystical&quot;, however a lot of the belief systems they embrace could be considered the opposite of that. Mystical thinking it's all about the magick comming from the inside, it's centered about the &quot;self empowerment&quot;, or cultivating a very direct connection to &quot;the divine&quot; to the point you don't need intermediaries at some point. But a lot of ideas about &quot;enligthenment&quot;, especially oriental ones, could be regarded as the <i>opposite </i>of that, as the &quot;self&quot; it's an illusion, the work it's centered not arround &quot;inner power&quot;, but rather about something that could be better regarded as &quot;freedom&quot;. Freedom to such an extreme extent as to want to be free from &quot;causality&quot; and even &quot;continuity&quot;.<br /> <br /> It could be cool if these types of belief had something &quot;paradox related&quot;. As you free yourself from the illusion of the world in different ways, you can flow trough it's mechanisms more skillfully","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1683,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","user":"Aleph","date":". 10-15-2024, 01:27 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","name":"Aleph","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3056"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-10-16T09:41:01-07:00","id":1543993,"title":"","content":"Some references:<br /> <br /> 1. What I've been referring to &quot;Wild Magick&quot; is the Optional Rule: Wild Talent on M20 pp.527\u2013528. Rules are very light: for a scene or two, the character commands a dice pool that's one to three higher than usual, accesses Spheres she doesn't have, and access more ranks in her existent Spheres than she has; the drawback is that the Storyteller makes all the decisions.<br /> <br /> 2. M20 p.534 gives us the Paradox acronyms. It stays that by default, Mage assumes HAB and PBD. Wild Talent is, almost by definition, an exception to this, and is much closer to RBD: the player states the results he's after, and the Storyteller decides how, or even if, the Magick achieves those results.<br /> <br /> I'll put some more thoughts here when I have more time.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":421,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","user":"Dataweaver","date":". 10-16-2024, 01:14 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-10-16T12:48:55-07:00","id":1544013,"title":"","content":"Well, I think it's a two-edged sword, in the sense that, while it serves to balance the setting, it also kind of encourages players to make magick as &quot;coincidences&quot; and things that can be explained in another way, what can be good or really really bad in the sens that the mage player throw any notion of paradigm through the window. I really hate this mentality because I think that even more important than paradox, it's the notion of paradigm to a mage, e.g. an hermetic mage should never try to make his spells look like what a scientifically oriented person would consider &quot;something normal&quot; or a &quot;coincidence&quot; because he/she lives in a world governed by the scieentific paradigm. So yes, it's important, but we need to be careful, otherwise the game &quot;stops being mage&quot; and becomes something else...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12348-herr-meister","name":"Herr Meister","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12348_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1114"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-10-17T07:18:58-07:00","id":1544101,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Herr Meister</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1543101-do-you-like-paradox?p=1544013#post1544013\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Well, I think it's a two-edged sword, in the sense that, while it serves to balance the setting, it also kind of encourages players to make magick as &quot;coincidences&quot; and things that can be explained in another way, what can be good or really really bad in the sens that the mage player throw any notion of paradigm through the window. I really hate this mentality because I think that even more important than paradox, it's the notion of paradigm to a mage, e.g. an hermetic mage should never try to make his spells look like what a scientifically oriented person would consider &quot;something normal&quot; or a &quot;coincidence&quot; because he/she lives in a world governed by the scieentific paradigm. So yes, it's important, but we need to be careful, otherwise the game &quot;stops being mage&quot; and becomes something else...</div> </div> </div> </div>So you assume mages dont know that consensus causes paradox? Cause if they know its only logical that they try to protect themselves by pretending","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28439-quelsec","name":"quelsec","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2024"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"407"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-10-17T12:11:50-07:00","id":1544127,"title":"","content":"Consensus doesn't cause Paradox, it modifies the risk of Paradox. Simple example: botching a roll in your Sanctum still generates Paradox. That's actually really important to keeping the feeling of &quot;Mage.&quot; Coincidental magic isn't about actually obeying Consensus/local Reality Zones, it's about being subtle enough to trick the system.<br /> <br /> That said, the books are very clear that mages are aware of said risks and most take steps to mitigate those risks.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-10-18T09:44:11-07:00","id":1544206,"title":"","content":"Indeed, there are a number of contributing factors to Paradox. The Consensus is one, but many mages suspect that the mage himself can trigger it through his own lack of belief. That's one of the suggested explanations for why Paradox can happen even when the magic doesn't contradict the reality zone. Likely this latter source of Paradox was the main source throughout most of history as mages didn't start noticing reliable paradox (then Scourge) trends until around the time the Ascension War started.<br /> <br /> I do think Paradox is a better term than Scourge, btw. Paradox implies the issue is a conflict between competing truths. It indicates that the products of awakened magic, the products of the consensus, and any underlying earthly foundations all have a claim on being the truth, even when they contradict.<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Mage: The Ice-ension: An Epic Game of Reality on the Rink","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/758-ramnesis","name":"Ramnesis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar758_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2220"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-10-18T19:08:02-07:00","id":1544248,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Herr Meister</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1543101-do-you-like-paradox?p=1544013#post1544013\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Well, I think it's a two-edged sword, in the sense that, while it serves to balance the setting, it also kind of encourages players to make magick as &quot;coincidences&quot; and things that can be explained in another way, what can be good or really really bad in the sens that the mage player throw any notion of paradigm through the window. I really hate this mentality because I think that even more important than paradox, it's the notion of paradigm to a mage, e.g. an hermetic mage should never try to make his spells look like what a scientifically oriented person would consider &quot;something normal&quot; or a &quot;coincidence&quot; because he/she lives in a world governed by the scieentific paradigm. So yes, it's important, but we need to be careful, otherwise the game &quot;stops being mage&quot; and becomes something else...</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes, that is something that mess a bit with mystical paradigms. They have a harder time hidding their magick and are forced to &quot;simulate&quot; scientific/technological explanations.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar617_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"617\" data-vbnamecard=\"617\">Heavy Arms</a>, I, disagree. Coincidental magick is about obeying consensus. &quot;Being subtle&quot; is about obeying the current consensus. If the consensus wasn't subtle (as it kinda was in dark ages), then not being subtle wouldn't generate paradox. The very concept if &quot;subtle&quot; is dictated by consensus.<br /> <br /> I see botches as the mage fucking up his attempt of doing magick, not related to consensus.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/758-ramnesis\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar758_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"758\" data-vbnamecard=\"758\">Ramnesis</a>, im not sure about botches beinf related to the mage lack of belief, is that from some book?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3153-lord-revan","name":"Lord Revan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3153_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1419"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-10-19T02:36:36-07:00","id":1544268,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lord Revan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1543101-do-you-like-paradox?p=1544248#post1544248\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar617_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"617\" data-vbnamecard=\"617\">Heavy Arms</a>, I, disagree. Coincidental magick is about obeying consensus. &quot;Being subtle&quot; is about obeying the current consensus. If the consensus wasn't subtle (as it kinda was in dark ages), then not being subtle wouldn't generate paradox. The very concept if &quot;subtle&quot; is dictated by consensus.</div> </div> </div> </div>This is explicitly not how the game is stated to work though.<br /> <br /> This is why M20 was very clear that the default mode of Mage is HAP not HOP: You don't need to obey the rules, you just need to be convincing enough to a HAP that you're not up to anything. A Hermetic that is quietly sitting at a cafe and toys with the gem on his ring that happens to coincide with a nearby car's alarm going off doesn't mean the mage is &quot;obeying&quot; Consenus by call on the sympathetic link of his gem and Forces to shake the car. It just means that your average person doesn't think a car alarm going off randomly is suspicious enough to have to be unnatural.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I see botches as the mage fucking up his attempt of doing magick, not related to consensus. </div> </div> </div>Then why do botches create the same amount of Paradox regardless of Consensus/Reality Zone?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-10-19T11:54:50-07:00","id":1544304,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1543101-do-you-like-paradox?p=1544268#post1544268\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> This is explicitly not how the game is stated to work though.<br /> <br /> This is why M20 was very clear that the default mode of Mage is HAP not HOP: You don't need to obey the rules, you just need to be convincing enough to a HAP that you're not up to anything. A Hermetic that is quietly sitting at a cafe and toys with the gem on his ring that happens to coincide with a nearby car's alarm going off doesn't mean the mage is &quot;obeying&quot; Consenus by call on the sympathetic link of his gem and Forces to shake the car. It just means that your average person doesn't think a car alarm going off randomly is suspicious enough to have to be unnatural.</div> </div> </div> </div>I believe we will have to define &quot;obeying consensus&quot;, then. To me, it means that you don't do anything that is considered impossible by the current scienctific knowledge. Your example is &quot;obeying consensus&quot; because a car alarm going off is acceptable by the scientific view, regardless if it was done by toying with a ring, using a wave emission machine or praying.<br /> <br /> Now, if instead of a car alarm you create a big explosion mid air, that is not obeying consensus, because science tells us that explosions just doesn't happen for no reason. So, if you toy with your ring and creates an explosion, consensus will make it vulgar. Now, if you use some sort of machine, that can be coincident, just because scientific view allow machines to create explosions.<br /> <br /> In older ages when magick was common (and the consensus was different), toying with your ring to create an explosion was acceptable.<br /> <br /> So, the point is that mages have to try and hide their effects (especially the blatant ones) with scientific explanations (which is the current consensus of M20) and that kinda suck for mystic mages. I believe that eas the point that Herr Meister was making.<br /> <br /> Idk, I guess I would like the concept of paradox and consensus better if that wasn't an issue. Maybe if the explanation was something more universal, same for mystic and technomancers.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1543101-do-you-like-paradox?p=1544268#post1544268\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Then why do botches create the same amount of Paradox regardless of Consensus/Reality Zone?</div> </div> </div> </div>Hum, didn't you just agree with me? Botches are independent of consensus/reality zones, and that's why I said it is caused by the mage doing a bad attempt of magick?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3153-lord-revan","name":"Lord Revan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3153_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1419"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-10-19T14:07:10-07:00","id":1544310,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lord Revan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1543101-do-you-like-paradox?p=1544304#post1544304\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I believe we will have to define &quot;obeying consensus&quot;, then. To me, it means that you don't do anything that is considered impossible by the current scienctific knowledge. Your example is &quot;obeying consensus&quot; because a car alarm going off is acceptable by the scientific view, regardless if it was done by toying with a ring, using a wave emission machine or praying.</div> </div> </div> </div>Except car alarms don't go off randomly according to Consensus. Car alarms only go off for specific reasons. Those reasons are just obscure enough that your average person isn't going to be suspicious if they don't immediately perceive it. That's the &quot;grey area&quot; the coincidental magic lives in. Using your gem inscribed with Enochian runes to call on the power of your will to shake a car does not make car alarms go off according to Consensus that is impossible to the scientific view. That's not obeying the laws of Consensus. Being subtle just tricks the &quot;eyes&quot; of Consensus to the fact that you're not obeying the rules because the result is subtle enough the HAP can't tell the difference (and why people consider HOP to make coincidental magic nearly impossible since a HOP can tell the difference).<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> So, the point is that mages have to try and hide their effects (especially the blatant ones) with scientific explanations (which is the current consensus of M20) and that kinda suck for mystic mages. I believe that eas the point that Herr Meister was making. </div> </div> </div>It's not though. He was arguing that a Hermetic stops being &quot;hermetic&quot; in their actions because they're being subtle in their manipulations of reality. Rubbing a mystic ring to manipulate Forces isn't &quot;giving in&quot; and making your character's paradigm the same as Consensus. It doesn't require a scientific explanation. It requires flying under the radar.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Idk, I guess I would like the concept of paradox and consensus better if that wasn't an issue. Maybe if the explanation was something more universal, same for mystic and technomancers. </div> </div> </div>The explanation is the same... Consensus has just been manipulated to favor some mages over others. That whole &quot;Ascension War&quot; thing. It's also why Reality Zones that don't follow Consensus can exist and flip the dynamic.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Hum, didn't you just agree with me? </div> </div> </div>Yes and no? You're arguing mutually contradictory positions: that Paradox is caused by Consensus and that Paradox is caused by something else.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-10-20T13:07:04-07:00","id":1544352,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1543101-do-you-like-paradox?p=1544310#post1544310\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Except car alarms don't go off randomly according to Consensus. Car alarms only go off for specific reasons. Those reasons are just obscure enough that your average person isn't going to be suspicious if they don't immediately perceive it. That's the &quot;grey area&quot; the coincidental magic lives in. Using your gem inscribed with Enochian runes to call on the power of your will to shake a car does not make car alarms go off according to Consensus that is impossible to the scientific view. That's not obeying the laws of Consensus. Being subtle just tricks the &quot;eyes&quot; of Consensus to the fact that you're not obeying the rules because the result is subtle enough the HAP can't tell the difference (and why people consider HOP to make coincidental magic nearly impossible since a HOP can tell the difference).</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, car alarms *do* goes off randomly as far as anyone can say. Sure, we know that something inside triggered it, but for us, it is basically random. The issue is that your car alarm example will *always* be coincident, due to how it is acceptable in the current consensus and it can go off randomly. So, the Hermetic with the ring would be as much coincidental as the technomancer wiith the wave emissor triggering it.<br /> <br /> Idk why you ignored my midair explosion example. In it, the Hermetic would certainly be vulgar with his ring, why the technomancer would be coincidental with his greande launcher. This is because of the consensus and means that consensus will determine if your spell is vulgar or not. If the consensus allowed sudden explosion in the air, both would be coincidental.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1543101-do-you-like-paradox?p=1544310#post1544310\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It's not though. He was arguing that a Hermetic stops being &quot;hermetic&quot; in their actions because they're being subtle in their manipulations of reality. Rubbing a mystic ring to manipulate Forces isn't &quot;giving in&quot; and making your character's paradigm the same as Consensus. It doesn't require a scientific explanation. It requires flying under the radar.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, they still believe in whatever they believe (mystical), but they do have to hide the effects under a scientific lens, which is the current consensus, to avoid paradox.<br /> <br /> &quot;Flying under the radar&quot; *is* providing a scientific explanation, especially for bigger effects. In fact, even the small effects work like that. A bystander that hear a car alarm go off just think &quot;well, must be some malfunction on the alarm&quot;, or &quot;damn cats jumping on cars&quot;. That is a scientific&quot; explanation.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1543101-do-you-like-paradox?p=1544310#post1544310\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The explanation is the same... Consensus has just been manipulated to favor some mages over others. That whole &quot;Ascension War&quot; thing. It's also why Reality Zones that don't follow Consensus can exist and flip the dynamic.</div> </div> </div> </div>Indeed, and here is where I'd like to expand this thread subject. I don't like the idea of reality &quot;getting back&quot; at the mage like some vengenful child. I also don't like reality trying to make things right and mundane by making even more vulgar effects, it makes no sense at all.<br /> <br /> Knowing that, M20 suggest for those who don't like that to keep paradox backlashes realistic and mainly just damage on the mage.<br /> <br /> <u>So, I'd like to know from you guys: How do you portray paradox in your games? How it works, how does it damages the mage? And do you keep it realistic or you go crazy with it? (I guess I already know the answers for that, lol)</u><br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1543101-do-you-like-paradox?p=1544310#post1544310\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yes and no? You're arguing mutually contradictory positions: that Paradox is caused by Consensus and that Paradox is caused by something else.</div> </div> </div> </div>[/quote]<br /> <br /> Yes, paradox is caused by consensus *and* paradox can be caused when the mage screws up his casting.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3153-lord-revan","name":"Lord Revan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3153_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1419"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-10-20T15:00:07-07:00","id":1544361,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lord Revan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1543101-do-you-like-paradox?p=1544352#post1544352\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Well, car alarms *do* goes off randomly as far as anyone can say.</div> </div> </div> </div>No, they don't. In reality car alarms go off for specific reasons that are not random.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> The issue is that your car alarm example will *always* be coincident, due to how it is acceptable in the current consensus and it can go off randomly. </div> </div> </div>So.... the problem with my example is that you're saying something that isn't true (that car alarms scientifically are triggered randomly)? Otherwise the idea that it's &quot;always&quot; coincidental isn't a problem. Though I object to the idea because we could always get better car alarms that are less likely to go off and it could shift from, &quot;car alarms are twitchy so seemingly random ones are normal,&quot; to something you only see in &quot;old&quot; cars and a new car having that happen would be perceived as vulgar. The perceptions of HAP can change over time. This is actually an example because newer alarms don't go off as readily as old ones did (because they actually hurt their intended purpose by being too sensitive and people starting ignoring them), but human perception hasn't caught up with that yet. It's very likely in 10-20 years (assuming the world hasn't gone off any multiple possible deep ends) this would be a vulgar effect for a mystic mage.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Idk why you ignored my midair explosion example. </div> </div> </div>Because it does nothing to illustrate the idea of what &quot;obeying&quot; the laws of Consensus means for a mystic mage compared to a technomancer. I can explore a car with a grenade launcher and I don't have magic powers of either sort. Using a tool that anyone can use in Consensus vs. using magic doesn't illustrate anything important to the discussion.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Well, they still believe in whatever they believe (mystical), but they do have to hide the effects under a scientific lens, which is the current consensus, to avoid paradox. </div> </div> </div>No, they have to hide their effects under the HAP lens, which as noted, is not strictly scientific. HAP doesn't have 5 dots in every knowledge, and it doesn't perceive every detail (that's what HOP does). It doesn't have to be strictly scientific, it just has to be good enough. That's also why even science based Focuses the Technocracy uses can still end up as vulgar effects when operating in Consensus: just because what they're doing might obey the laws of science in a fashion genius experts can understand doesn't mean average people are going to think it's plausible for someone to do that yet. Even Technocrats have to &quot;fly under the radar.&quot;<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> &quot;Flying under the radar&quot; *is* providing a scientific explanation, especially for bigger effects. </div> </div> </div>Nope, see above.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> That is a scientific&quot; explanation. </div> </div> </div>No, it very much is not. Those are rationalizations made by people that are trained to perceive the world defined by scientific parameters, not actual scientific explanations.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I don't like the idea of reality &quot;getting back&quot; at the mage like some vengenful child. </div> </div> </div>Who is advocating for that exactly? Including the books. Scourge, the Sorcerer's Crusade era take on Paradox, was presented as proof that backlashes themselves are a fundamental part of Awakened magic, but their manifestations are filtered through Reality Zones and thus while there will always be some form of it that originates from an impartial fundamental aspect of how realty warping magic works, it can seem &quot;vengeful&quot; if local Reality says it should look that way.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <u>So, I'd like to know from you guys: How do you portray paradox in your games? How it works, how does it damages the mage? And do you keep it realistic or you go crazy with it? (I guess I already know the answers for that, lol)</u> </div> </div> </div>Um, you're using such vague language here it's nearly impossible to answer.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Yes, paradox is caused by consensus *and* paradox can be caused when the mage screws up his casting. </div> </div> </div>By what mechanism? Where is it ever stated that this is the case?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-10-20T17:01:20-07:00","id":1544364,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lord Revan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1543101-do-you-like-paradox?p=1543301#post1543301\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar1683_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"1683\" data-vbnamecard=\"1683\">Aleph</a> , very well put. I agree with practically everything and now I understand what you mean by &quot;it's not a limitation&quot;. Actually, as <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar5826_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"5826\" data-vbnamecard=\"5826\">monteparnas</a> , it is a different kind of limitation. One where you can keeps casting whenever you want regardless of &quot;points&quot;.<br /> <br /> I just have some observations:<br /> <br /> - The Technocracy is as strong as the ST wants it to be, so it *might* be a limitng factor or not so muuch<br /> <br /> - Unlike the Masquerade or Veil, it isn't considered a &quot;crime&quot; by his peers for mages to cast vulgar spells, quite the contrary, it is &quot;encouraged&quot; as a way to change consensus<br /> <br /> - There could be a system of points/mana that isn't limited daily. For example, the mage could regain points by minutes/hours, or in some other ways, like meditating or something to restore points. Tbh, D&amp;D is quire like that, since casters can rest and restore their spells (of course, some DMs might limit resting).<br /> <br /> So, do you think there is a better system of keeping magick on track? Have this ever been tought about by you guys?<br /> <br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/758-ramnesis\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar758_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"758\" data-vbnamecard=\"758\">Ramnesis</a> , I share some of your opinons. I'm not sure magick should be unpredictable or risky, just hard and maybe exhausting. And one thing I don't like at all is the unbelief rule, especially because there isnt one and it's just too vague...</div> </div> </div> </div>Gurps use Fatigue Points, and you naturally recover 1 point every 10 minutes that you're not exerting yourself. So yes, there are many ways.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28035-magus-maximus","name":"Magus Maximus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2023"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"569"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-10-21T10:24:28-07:00","id":1544406,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1543101-do-you-like-paradox?p=1544361#post1544361\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> No, they don't. In reality car alarms go off for specific reasons that are not random.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> So.... the problem with my example is that you're saying something that isn't true (that car alarms scientifically are triggered randomly)? Otherwise the idea that it's &quot;always&quot; coincidental isn't a problem. Though I object to the idea because we could always get better car alarms that are less likely to go off and it could shift from, &quot;car alarms are twitchy so seemingly random ones are normal,&quot; to something you only see in &quot;old&quot; cars and a new car having that happen would be perceived as vulgar. The perceptions of HAP can change over time. This is actually an example because newer alarms don't go off as readily as old ones did (because they actually hurt their intended purpose by being too sensitive and people starting ignoring them), but human perception hasn't caught up with that yet. It's very likely in 10-20 years (assuming the world hasn't gone off any multiple possible deep ends) this would be a vulgar effect for a mystic mage.</div> </div> </div> </div>I know, and said, that car alarms go off for specific reasons and are not random. I was talking about the bystander perception. Very often we hear car alarms trigger and there is no one robbing the car. It seems that it has triggered by nothing at all, while we *know* that something has triggered it (otherwise it wouldn't go off). <br /> <br /> Your example is bad because, as right now, no one would say that a car alarm triggering would be impossible. Ever. You could wave your hands, toy with your ring, shout enochian words and point at the car, and at that exact moment trigger the alarm. Still, the HAP would say &quot;it was a coincidence&quot;, because cara alarms are that bad.<br /> <br /> Sure, in a world where 99% of car alarms only goes off in case of robery, then consensus is different and your magick might be vulgar. But then, that just proves my point that consensus affect paradox.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1543101-do-you-like-paradox?p=1544361#post1544361\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Because it does nothing to illustrate the idea of what &quot;obeying&quot; the laws of Consensus means for a mystic mage compared to a technomancer. I can explore a car with a grenade launcher and I don't have magic powers of either sort. Using a tool that anyone can use in Consensus vs. using magic doesn't illustrate anything important to the discussion.</div> </div> </div> </div>Ok, you can exchange a grenade launcher with a quantum wave fluctuator that transforms air into hot plasma and creates explosions (or whatever). My point is that you have to argue with vulgar effects and not coincidental ones.<br /> <br /> You can choose any *vulgar* effect, if you want, and you will see that the technomancer has a waaay easier time going coincidental with it, than the mystic mage. This is stated clearly in M20, that's the advantage technomancers have over mystics (and mystics advantage is dropping instruments earlier).<br /> <br /> And they have this advantage <b>because their paradigm is more in line with the current consensus, which means consensus affects paradox directly.</b><br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1543101-do-you-like-paradox?p=1544361#post1544361\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">No, they have to hide their effects under the HAP lens, which as noted, is not strictly scientific. HAP doesn't have 5 dots in every knowledge, and it doesn't perceive every detail (that's what HOP does). It doesn't have to be strictly scientific, it just has to be good enough. That's also why even science based Focuses the Technocracy uses can still end up as vulgar effects when operating in Consensus: just because what they're doing might obey the laws of science in a fashion genius experts can understand doesn't mean average people are going to think it's plausible for someone to do that yet. Even Technocrats have to &quot;fly under the radar.&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>Again, you are missing my point. Of course the average HAP doesn't know everything about science (quite the contrary), but he knows at least a bit. Enough to force all mages that want to go coincident to create an explanation (even a BS one) for their effects. <br /> <br /> Again &quot;HAP lens&quot;, &quot;obeying consensus&quot;, &quot;flying under the radar&quot; are the same thing: make your effects seem plausible for an HAP. And that means, having *some* sort of scientific explanation for your effect. Not technocracy Science!, not technomancer Science!, but real, current world, mundane science. <br /> If your effect doesn't fit into the sleepers scientific view, it will probably be vulgar (except reality zones, etc.)<br /> And the technos paradigm is much closer to that sleeper science than the mystical hermetic.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1543101-do-you-like-paradox?p=1544361#post1544361\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">No, it very much is not. Those are rationalizations made by people that are trained to perceive the world defined by scientific parameters, not actual scientific explanations.</div> </div> </div> </div>You want to go that way? Fair enough. Then to get coincident a mage needs to fit: &quot;rationalizations made by people that are trained to perceive the world defined by scientific parameters&quot;, and the hermetic mage would have to &quot;give&quot; an explanation that fits the world defined scientific parameters, which might be very different from his real paradigm, while the technos wouldn't have to change his own view too much, to reach such an explanation.<br /> <br /> That would be very clear when we work with a vulgar example.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1543101-do-you-like-paradox?p=1544361#post1544361\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Who is advocating for that exactly? Including the books. Scourge, the Sorcerer's Crusade era take on Paradox, was presented as proof that backlashes themselves are a fundamental part of Awakened magic, but their manifestations are filtered through Reality Zones and thus while there will always be some form of it that originates from an impartial fundamental aspect of how realty warping magic works, it can seem &quot;vengeful&quot; if local Reality says it should look that way.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, paradox &quot;gets back&quot; in backlashes, that's a fact. The vengenful child was on me, because that's the feeling I have. I don't like paradox creating vulgar effects.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1543101-do-you-like-paradox?p=1544361#post1544361\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Um, you're using such vague language here it's nearly impossible to answer.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, do you use paradox flaws in a vulgar way? When the mage takes damage from paradox backlashes, how do you describe it (burning tissue, electric shocks, opening wounds)?<br /> When a mage is gathering paradox or getting a backlash, there is some visual effect for the paradox?<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1543101-do-you-like-paradox?p=1544361#post1544361\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">By what mechanism? Where is it ever stated that this is the case?</div> </div> </div> </div>I believe it is not. That is my view of botched paradox. Since botches means that you failed miserably on your attempt of doing something, botching Arete means that the mage failed to cast and gets more paradox because of that. <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3153-lord-revan","name":"Lord Revan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3153_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1419"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-10-21T10:34:21-07:00","id":1544409,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Magus Maximus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1543101-do-you-like-paradox?p=1544364#post1544364\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Gurps use Fatigue Points, and you naturally recover 1 point every 10 minutes that you're not exerting yourself. So yes, there are many ways.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, that would be a simpler but effective way of doing it. But then, mages would lose that capacity of &quot;constantly casting&quot; that they theoretically have (if you don't mind paradox), I guess. <br /> <br /> Tbh, I do like that perk of M20, my only issue is how paradox is portraied in-game. I would rather keep the paradox system, but having no vulgar backlashes. And maybe change the explanation, like when you alter reality you exert yourself and the more you alter the more you get tired (or something of the sort), to the point that you get damage when doing too much magick.<br /> <br /> The exerting explanation, however, wouldn't make sense to be gathered in a paradox wheel, it would have to always backlash on casting, which means always a low damage...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3153-lord-revan","name":"Lord Revan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3153_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1419"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-10-21T13:38:15-07:00","id":1544426,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lord Revan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1543101-do-you-like-paradox?p=1544409#post1544409\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Yeah, that would be a simpler but effective way of doing it. But then, mages would lose that capacity of &quot;constantly casting&quot; that they theoretically have (if you don't mind paradox), I guess.<br /> <br /> Tbh, I do like that perk of M20, my only issue is how paradox is portraied in-game. I would rather keep the paradox system, but having no vulgar backlashes. And maybe change the explanation, like when you alter reality you exert yourself and the more you alter the more you get tired (or something of the sort), to the point that you get damage when doing too much magick.<br /> <br /> The exerting explanation, however, wouldn't make sense to be gathered in a paradox wheel, it would have to always backlash on casting, which means always a low damage...</div> </div> </div> </div>Get the book &quot;Gurps Thaumatology&quot;. It is basically a toolkit on how to build your very own Magic System for Game Mechanics. You don't need to understand Gurps to make use of it. In it you have ideas such as, for instance, a system of &quot;tally&quot; - that is, you can cast magic willy nilly up to a certain point, after which, if you continue, bad things will happen.<br /> <br /> Or, you can accrue &quot;Corruption Points&quot;, for systems upon which Magic is a sort of evil power, and using it too much brings bad things upon your head (of the cursed kind of bad things). Very good for Horror games, of the sort of Call of Cthulhu.<br /> <br /> With Gurps Thaumatology you can actually recreate Mage the Ascension Game Mechanics from scratch for ANY OTHER SYSTEM. Or you can also modify it.<br /> <br /> I use it extensively in order to make things like personalized Spheres, with groups having merely 7 Spheres (my Technocrats are like that), some others have 3 (my Dreamspeakers are like that) and also having sub-spheres or &quot;special&quot; ones (like the &quot;Sphere of Alchemy&quot; and &quot;Necromancy&quot; or the Sub-spheres of Pyromancy and Cryomancy, Plant Sphere and I even have the Sphere of Memetics).<br /> <br /> If you like toying with mechanics, that book is a good source<br /> <br /> Edit: now I've read all that you said, Gurps has a few systems that could embark what you're asking, with just some small tweaks to function for D10 system. Fatigue like I said is one possibility. In Gurps you can also &quot;buy&quot; limitations (sort of like &quot;flaws&quot;) to use Hit Points instead of Fatigue. You can also already use your own Hit Points once your Fatigue is spent. That would function like what you're asking. <br /> <br /> But there's much more","signature":"","edited":{"userid":28035,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28035-magus-maximus","user":"Magus Maximus","date":". 10-21-2024, 04:43 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28035-magus-maximus","name":"Magus Maximus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2023"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"569"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-10-21T13:56:33-07:00","id":1544429,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lord Revan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1543101-do-you-like-paradox?p=1544406#post1544406\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I know, and said, that car alarms go off for specific reasons and are not random.</div> </div> </div> </div>No, that's what I said. You said, &quot;Well, car alarms *do* goes off randomly as far as anyone can say.&quot;<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I was talking about the bystander perception. Very often we hear car alarms trigger and there is no one robbing the car. It seems that it has triggered by nothing at all, while we *know* that something has triggered it (otherwise it wouldn't go off). </div> </div> </div>We also know that rubbing a ring with magical sigils on it is not one of the reasons car alarms go off, but you're accepting that it's coincidental for that to be the cause of a car alarm going off under Consensus.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Your example is bad because, as right now, no one would say that a car alarm triggering would be impossible. Ever. </div> </div> </div>My mage levitates the car and shakes it until the alarm goes off.<br /> <br /> My mage makes a demonstration of removing the battery, proving that the alarm is disabled by doing things that should set it off, and then makes it go off using magic.<br /> <br /> Etc.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> But then, that just proves my point that consensus affect paradox. </div> </div> </div>No, that <b>was my point</b> you were claiming that <u>Consensus <b>causes</b> Paradox</u>.<br /> <br /> Maybe you need to go reread your own damned posts since you seem to be confusing my point (that Consensus only varies Paradox, not causes it) for your posts (which assert that Consensus causes Paradox).<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Ok, you can exchange a grenade launcher with a quantum wave fluctuator that transforms air into hot plasma and creates explosions (or whatever). My point is that you have to argue with vulgar effects and not coincidental ones. </div> </div> </div>Transforming air into hot plasma would be vulgar, even for a Technocrat, because directed plasma weapons aren't part of Consensus (yet anyway).<br /> <br /> And you haven't made any sort of logical case why coincidental effects don't matter, and only vulgar effects matter... especially since there's very few things that are actually 100% coincidental or 100% vulgar. &gt;99.99% of magic in the game is maybe one or the other depending on circumstance.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> You can choose any *vulgar* effect, if you want, and you will see that the technomancer has a waaay easier time going coincidental with it, than the mystic mage. </div> </div> </div>You're thinking is backwards. There's not such things as &quot;vulgar effects&quot; that Technomancers have an easier time &quot;going coincidental.&quot; Technomancers have an easier time achieving their goals with coincidental magic because their paradigm's closer alignment to Consensus means they can do more while staying coincidental. They don't transform vulgar magic into coincidental magic. It was always coincidental for them in Consensus.<br /> <br /> The whole point since the beginnings of Mage, has not been to &quot;turn vulgar magic coincidental,&quot; but rather to come up with coincidental expressions of magic if you want to avoid Paradox and exposure. And no, they are not the same thing. Asserting words mean the same thing even though they don't doesn't &quot;win&quot; the Internet no matter how often you try.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> This is stated clearly in M20, that's the advantage technomancers have over mystics (and mystics advantage is dropping instruments earlier). </div> </div> </div>This was never in contention. You're making up disagreements to &quot;win&quot; debate points that were never brought up until you did. This is bad argumentation.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Again &quot;HAP lens&quot;, &quot;obeying consensus&quot;, &quot;flying under the radar&quot; are the same thing: </div> </div> </div>No, they aren't. This is just proof that when you said &quot;define obey Cosensus&quot; you meant, &quot;Words mean whatever I want them to to win Internet debates, and those that disagree are fucking losers.&quot;<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> And that means, having *some* sort of scientific explanation for your effect. Not technocracy Science!, not technomancer Science!, but real, current world, mundane science. </div> </div> </div>What, exactly, is the real, current world, mundane scientific explanation for how rubbing a gem on a ring inscribed with Enochian sigils causes car alarms to go off?<br /> <br /> There isn't one. That's why you're wrong, and why you're resorting to such pathetic and asinine rheotrical jokes as if they were intelligent responses.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Well, paradox &quot;gets back&quot; in backlashes, that's a fact. </div> </div> </div>That's like the sun &quot;gets back&quot; at people in the form of sun burn and skin cancer.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I don't like paradox creating vulgar effects. </div> </div> </div>It doesn't do that. Vulgar effects generate Paradox, not the other way around.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Well, do you use paradox flaws in a vulgar way? </div> </div> </div>Paradox Flaws are not Awakened magic and thus are neither coincidental or vulgar. They're supernatural, and can be obvious, and I have used them as such, but like I said, your wording makes this discussion more difficult even when it's not bad faith lying about posts.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> When the mage takes damage from paradox backlashes, how do you describe it (burning tissue, electric shocks, opening wounds)? </div> </div> </div>Variable.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> When a mage is gathering paradox or getting a backlash, there is some visual effect for the paradox? </div> </div> </div>As there's nothing in the books that indicates a visual/mundane-sensory aspect to Paradox, I don't include those. Sleepers can't &quot;see&quot; Paradox gathering, though they might see the results of a backlash depending on what happened.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> That is my view of botched paradox. </div> </div> </div>Clearly you've botching your rolls to make your views on Paradox good discussion points.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-10-22T12:00:27-07:00","id":1544481,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1543101-do-you-like-paradox?p=1544429#post1544429\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">No, that's what I said. You said, &quot;Well, car alarms *do* goes off randomly as far as anyone can say.&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes. key words here are &quot;as far as anyone can say&quot;. Because of all the hundreds of times I've heard a car alarm trigger, it wasn't a robery and I couldn't say why it was screaming. So, to me (a HAP) it was random (even though I know that in reality something must have triggered it), got it?<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1543101-do-you-like-paradox?p=1544429#post1544429\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">We also know that rubbing a ring with magical sigils on it is not one of the reasons car alarms go off, but you're accepting that it's coincidental for that to be the cause of a car alarm going off under Consensus.</div> </div> </div> </div>Again, your example is terrible, because car alarms are constantly triggering for no APARENT reason. You could use your argument about mind reading, which is also almost always coincident.<br /> You would have to be very creative to make those effects in a vulgar way.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1543101-do-you-like-paradox?p=1544429#post1544429\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">My mage levitates the car and shakes it until the alarm goes off.<br /> <br /> My mage makes a demonstration of removing the battery, proving that the alarm is disabled by doing things that should set it off, and then makes it go off using magic.<br /> <br /> Etc.</div> </div> </div> </div>I..didn't get your point here...Are you trying to make the effect vulgar? Levitation is vulgar, yeah, and a a totally different effect.<br /> Removing the battery would make a HAP think that there is some sort of trick or backup battery or whatever to keep the alarm on. It would be very hard to make this effect vulgar. Which doen't mean you can't...<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1543101-do-you-like-paradox?p=1544429#post1544429\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">No, that <b>was my point</b> you were claiming that <u>Consensus <b>causes</b> Paradox</u>.<br /> Maybe you need to go reread your own damned posts since you seem to be confusing my point (that Consensus only varies Paradox, not causes it) for your posts (which assert that Consensus causes Paradox).</div> </div> </div> </div>You should go back and reread as well, because I never said that consensus caused paradox. I said that I disagree with your first post, where you said that coincidental magick isn't about obeying consensus. Of course that what causes paradox is vulgar magick. And vulgar magick is dictated by the current consensus. So, while consensus per se doesn't *causes* paradox, it is heavily related to it. Maybe we agree on that and are arguing needlessly?<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1543101-do-you-like-paradox?p=1544429#post1544429\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Transforming air into hot plasma would be vulgar, even for a Technocrat, because directed plasma weapons aren't part of Consensus (yet anyway).<br /> <br /> And you haven't made any sort of logical case why coincidental effects don't matter, and only vulgar effects matter... especially since there's very few things that are actually 100% coincidental or 100% vulgar. &gt;99.99% of magic in the game is maybe one or the other depending on circumstance.</div> </div> </div> </div>Because there are effects that are so subtle that any focus in any consensus would be coincident (like your alarm example), and we are trying to compare mystics and technos. If we use examples where both can easily make coincident, we won't make a complete analysis of how easy it is for each. We need blatant, vulgar effects as examples.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1543101-do-you-like-paradox?p=1544429#post1544429\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You're thinking is backwards. There's not such things as &quot;vulgar effects&quot; that Technomancers have an easier time &quot;going coincidental.&quot; Technomancers have an easier time achieving their goals with coincidental magic because their paradigm's closer alignment to Consensus means they can do more while staying coincidental. They don't transform vulgar magic into coincidental magic. It was always coincidental for them in Consensus.<br /> <br /> The whole point since the beginnings of Mage, has not been to &quot;turn vulgar magic coincidental,&quot; but rather to come up with coincidental expressions of magic if you want to avoid Paradox and exposure. And no, they are not the same thing. Asserting words mean the same thing even though they don't doesn't &quot;win&quot; the Internet no matter how often you try.<br /> This was never in contention. You're making up disagreements to &quot;win&quot; debate points that were never brought up until you did. This is bad argumentation.</div> </div> </div> </div>First of all, Im not here to &quot;win internet points&quot; how old do you think I am?<br /> <br /> &quot;Technomancers have an easier time achieving their goals with coincidental magic because their paradigm's closer alignment to Consensus means they can do more while staying coincidental.&quot;<br /> <br /> This right here is what I was saying, with other, simpler words. And Herr argument was that the hermetic have to adapt to that current consensus (scientific) to &quot;align&quot; their effects to what is considered plausible or risk going vulgar. While technos don't need to do that as much. That's it.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1543101-do-you-like-paradox?p=1544429#post1544429\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">No, they aren't. This is just proof that when you said &quot;define obey Cosensus&quot; you meant, &quot;Words mean whatever I want them to to win Internet debates, and those that disagree are fucking losers.&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>Dude, are you ok? Are you fucking drunk? I never said that, nor called anyone a loser. To me, all those terms means exactly what you posted above: align your effect with consensus to hide it as coincident.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1543101-do-you-like-paradox?p=1544429#post1544429\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What, exactly, is the real, current world, mundane scientific explanation for how rubbing a gem on a ring inscribed with Enochian sigils causes car alarms to go off?<br /> <br /> There isn't one. That's why you're wrong, and why you're resorting to such pathetic and asinine rheotrical jokes as if they were intelligent responses.</div> </div> </div> </div>Since you are clearly drunk, I will ignore the offenses. Yes, there is no sleeper scientific explanation, and that's why, if you gave a better/more blatant example, it would be vulgar. And that's my point.<br /> Rubbing your ring to make a car alarm trigger might be coincident, because car alarms are that lame. Rubbing your ring to explode the car would be vulgar, while the techno can explode the car in 1001 different ways and still keep it coincident.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1543101-do-you-like-paradox?p=1544429#post1544429\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That's like the sun &quot;gets back&quot; at people in the form of sun burn and skin cancer.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's a cool way to see it. Some sort of physical consequence. For Paradox start to make sense to me, the backlashes would have to have a connection with the effect or the mage. I'll explain more bellow.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1543101-do-you-like-paradox?p=1544429#post1544429\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It doesn't do that. Vulgar effects generate Paradox, not the other way around.<br /> Paradox Flaws are not Awakened magic and thus are neither coincidental or vulgar. They're supernatural, and can be obvious, and I have used them as such, but like I said, your wording makes this discussion more difficult even when it's not bad faith lying about posts.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, it's not bad faith. What I meant was that I don't like backlashes that are not on par with the consensus. For the examples in M20, you can grow big ass horns. I don't like reality trying to correct the mage's attempt of disrupting the consensus by making *more* blatant stuff, like growing horns.<br /> I think in M20 paradox backlashes are described too vaguely, they do not seems (at least I don't remember reading) to create a direct relation between the mage, the effect and the backlash. I mean, why would Reality grow horns on the mage's head? Unless he was trying to transform himself into some kind of animal, I see no sense in that.<br /> More than that, growing horns on someone's head is completely against the consensus and Reality trying to fix consensus by breaking consensus makes no sense at all. The same goes for Paradox Spirits, at least in my opinion.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3153-lord-revan","name":"Lord Revan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3153_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1419"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-10-22T12:08:32-07:00","id":1544482,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Magus Maximus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1543101-do-you-like-paradox?p=1544426#post1544426\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Get the book &quot;Gurps Thaumatology&quot;. It is basically a toolkit on how to build your very own Magic System for Game Mechanics. You don't need to understand Gurps to make use of it. In it you have ideas such as, for instance, a system of &quot;tally&quot; - that is, you can cast magic willy nilly up to a certain point, after which, if you continue, bad things will happen.<br /> <br /> Or, you can accrue &quot;Corruption Points&quot;, for systems upon which Magic is a sort of evil power, and using it too much brings bad things upon your head (of the cursed kind of bad things). Very good for Horror games, of the sort of Call of Cthulhu.<br /> <br /> With Gurps Thaumatology you can actually recreate Mage the Ascension Game Mechanics from scratch for ANY OTHER SYSTEM. Or you can also modify it.<br /> <br /> I use it extensively in order to make things like personalized Spheres, with groups having merely 7 Spheres (my Technocrats are like that), some others have 3 (my Dreamspeakers are like that) and also having sub-spheres or &quot;special&quot; ones (like the &quot;Sphere of Alchemy&quot; and &quot;Necromancy&quot; or the Sub-spheres of Pyromancy and Cryomancy, Plant Sphere and I even have the Sphere of Memetics).<br /> <br /> If you like toying with mechanics, that book is a good source<br /> <br /> Edit: now I've read all that you said, Gurps has a few systems that could embark what you're asking, with just some small tweaks to function for D10 system. Fatigue like I said is one possibility. In Gurps you can also &quot;buy&quot; limitations (sort of like &quot;flaws&quot;) to use Hit Points instead of Fatigue. You can also already use your own Hit Points once your Fatigue is spent. That would function like what you're asking.<br /> <br /> But there's much more</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, the options seems endless. A lot of what you said kinda look like M20, more or less. Even the idea of using HP for casting (if you have Prime 1), lol.<br /> I will take a look at this book later, but I'd rather try to find some way of making sense of paradox in-game before.<br /> <br /> I think that getting rid of consensus breaking backlashes is the most important. Maybe paradox spirits too...<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3153-lord-revan","name":"Lord Revan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3153_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1419"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-10-22T13:45:21-07:00","id":1544495,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lord Revan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1543101-do-you-like-paradox?p=1544481#post1544481\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yes. key words here are &quot;as far as anyone can say&quot;.</div> </div> </div> </div>&quot;Anyone&quot; includes above average people that could say it was impossible. HAP isn't &quot;as far as anyone can say,&quot; but, &quot;as far as the average person could say.&quot;<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Again, your example is terrible, because car alarms are constantly triggering for no APARENT reason. </div> </div> </div>Except that isn't actually true.<br /> <br /> Besides that, it doesn't really hurt my argument at all. Because the fact that average perception is <b>NOT SCIENTIFIC </b>refutes statements that coincidental magic has to provide a scientific explanation for how it's not vulgar.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I..didn't get your point here...Are you trying to make the effect vulgar? </div> </div> </div>Yes, to refute your statement that it would be difficult to do so.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> You should go back and reread as well, because I never said that consensus caused paradox. </div> </div> </div>Wow, you deleted a post and didn't bother editing the next post where you said, &quot;Yes, paradox is caused by consensus...&quot;<br /> <br /> Take your gaslighting BS and shove it.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I said that I disagree with your first post, where you said that coincidental magick isn't about obeying consensus. Of course that what causes paradox is vulgar magick. And vulgar magick is dictated by the current consensus. So, while consensus per se doesn't *causes* paradox, it is heavily related to it. Maybe we agree on that and are arguing needlessly? </div> </div> </div>1) There's massive holes in your logic that never gets back to the whole &quot;obeying&quot; thing (and when you got back to that in previous posts you just played semantic games). Lets try something simple: Is driving 26 mph in an area with a 25 mph speed limit obeying traffic laws, or is it violating traffic laws even if by such a small degree that the odds of getting a ticket are negligible?<br /> <br /> 2) What causes Paradox is Awakened magic screwing with Reality. Vulgar magic increases the potential for local Reality to snap back to normal in a fashion harmful to the mage, but the 'snap back' is why magic that isn't vulgar can still generate Paradox, and why witnesses impact the potential snap back as well.<br /> <br /> 3) The only needless things are your overt lies.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> ...and we are trying to compare mystics and technos. </div> </div> </div>No, you are because you don't like what happens if we don't constrain the discussion to your chosen criteria.<br /> <br /> The point started by a different poster, was that mystic mages don't feel like they have a real Focus when the game stresses coincidental magic so much because they have to act like technos to be coincidental. Your sidetracking about vulgar magic is, in fact, bullshit.<br /> <br /> The point of focusing on coincidental magic is that Focus still matters to mystic mages because they don't do techno style magic when doing coincidental magic. They still do mystic magic. This is the whole &quot;obey vs. subtle&quot; debate in a nutshell. Doing small subtle changes isn't turning a mystic into a techno, it's just being subtle enough people don't see what you're doing. Obeying would mean becoming a techno because you'd be doing things according to Consensus's rules, not taking advantage of Consensus's blind spots.<br /> <br /> Analysis of anything beyond that is a distraction.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> First of all, Im not here to &quot;win internet points&quot; how old do you think I am? </div> </div> </div>Your biological age clearly doesn't stop you from trying to manipulating the conversation, lie, and other bullshit that has no clear motivation besides Internet pettiness. You could be 50, and it wouldn't stop you from acting like a particularly bratty 8 year old.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> This right here is what I was saying, with other, simpler words. </div> </div> </div>So, I'm right, your wrong, but your desire for Internet points is stopping you from just admitting it.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Dude, are you ok? </div> </div> </div>Yes, I'm not the only lying to people on the Internet because I said something stupid on a forum about a game.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Are you fucking drunk? </div> </div> </div>I wish, it would make dealing with your crap easier.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> To me, all those terms means exactly what you posted above: align your effect with consensus to hide it as coincident. </div> </div> </div>Then my point stands. You don't care about what the words actually mean, you only care about bending twisting them to make yourself &quot;right&quot; on the Internet.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Since you are clearly drunk, I will ignore the offenses. </div> </div> </div>Wow, how mature, &quot;I'm going to take the high ground by insulting you too!&quot; When you catch me lying, try again, liar.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Yes, there is no sleeper scientific explanation, and that's why, if you gave a better/more blatant example, it would be vulgar. And that's my point. </div> </div> </div>And yet again, you contradict yourself. &quot;Flying under the radar&quot; *is* providing a scientific explanation...&quot; you can't keep your arguments straight, and instead of trying to get better arguments, you lie about it.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Rubbing your ring to explode the car would be vulgar, while the techno can explode the car in 1001 different ways and still keep it coincident. </div> </div> </div>Not really, because cars don't explode on a regular enough basis for people to consider a car just exploding to be normal. Like your grenade launcher quip, the &quot;1001&quot; ways are just not using magic, or using magic to do something they could have done without it. The work to make it coincidental is greater than the work to do it mundanely.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Yeah, it's not bad faith. </div> </div> </div>No, the lying is bad faith.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I don't like reality trying to correct the mage's attempt of disrupting the consensus by making *more* blatant stuff, like growing horns. </div> </div> </div>That presumes Reality is a thinking entity in Mage.<br /> <br /> When you get a cut, you don't just heal back with fresh skin. You get scabs, you risk infections and your body responds with inflammation, etc. The worse the cut, the more your body does beyond grow new skin to seal the cut.<br /> <br /> Horns are like a nasty scab. It's a big ass sign something wrong happened, that's part of the process of getting back to just skin.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I think in M20 paradox backlashes are described too vaguely, they do not seems (at least I don't remember reading) to create a direct relation between the mage, the effect and the backlash. </div> </div> </div>M20 leaves a lot of it up to the ST to decide for the tone of their own games, and because M20 was trying to remain appealing to multiple editions of the game which had their own peculiarities in this arena (1e/2e was much more &quot;punishment motivated&quot; Paradox, while Revised was more &quot;natural force of metaphysics&quot; Paradox).<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\ude00","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-10-22T14:06:08-07:00","id":1544498,"title":"","content":"I would recommend <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/446015\" target=\"_blank\">Prism of Focus</a> for the matter of ways that Paradox manifests. In particular, it does a rundown of the various Practices with, among other things, ideas of what Paradox looks like when using the Practice in question.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-10-22T15:02:09-07:00","id":1544505,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lord Revan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1543101-do-you-like-paradox?p=1544482#post1544482\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I think that getting rid of consensus breaking backlashes is the most important. Maybe paradox spirits too...<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>So, like making backlashes function like ERASERS of &quot;reality offenses&quot; rather than totally random nonsense?<br /> <br /> So, instead of making someone turn into a fly because they turned lead into gold, how about if the Mage's bank account gets emptied?<br /> <br /> I like this idea and I agree with you, backlashes should be a sort of attempt from reality to fix itself, so my suggestion would be not to do it tip for tat, but rather to make &quot;metaphysical fixes&quot;.<br /> <br /> I'll explain: the bank account is a good example. Monetary value being created out of the blue is a big no no for momma Consensus, so it &quot;fixes&quot; it by taking it out of somewhere else.<br /> <br /> Healing magics for instance, could make the Mage turn into a carrier of a new magic disease (which he himself is immune). Father Consensus conservates therefore the balance between Healthy (all the unsanctioned healing magics performed improving the health status of living beings) with unhealthy by creating diseases. Healers thus have to be aware not to turn into plague carriers.<br /> <br /> And so on so forth. As a plus, this follows the 3 rules of magic of the Corpus Hermeticum (the real life one), such as the law of Contagion.<br /> <br /> We can keep thinking on similar examples, but it's doable","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28035-magus-maximus","name":"Magus Maximus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2023"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"569"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-10-22T17:03:30-07:00","id":1544520,"title":"","content":"<b><span style=\"color:#c0392b\">Please refrain from disrespectful, insulting, and accusatory posts. Familiarize yourself with our <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\">forum rules</a> and take a break from the topic if you're getting upset. Warnings have been issued.</span></b>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/They<br /> Moderator<br /> Line Developer: <b><a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/browse/pub/4261/Onyx-Path-Publishing/subcategory/8329_24824/Scarred-Lands-new\" target=\"_blank\">Scarred Lands</a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25411-travislegge","name":"TravisLegge","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25411_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"227"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-10-23T09:21:13-07:00","id":1544566,"title":"","content":"<span style=\"font-family:Calibri\"><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1543101-do-you-like-paradox?p=1544495#post1544495\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> &quot;Anyone&quot; includes above average people that could say it was impossible. HAP isn't &quot;as far as anyone can say,&quot; but, &quot;as far as the average person could say.&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Calibri\">Ok, my point stands. An average person wouldn\u2019t know why the car triggered and will create all sort of rationalization, and thus, the effect is coincident.<br /> <br /> <br /> [QUOTE=Heavy Arms;n1544495]<br /> Except that isn't actually true.<br /> <br /> Besides that, it doesn't really hurt my argument at all. Because the fact that average perception is <b>NOT SCIENTIFIC </b>refutes statements that coincidental magic has to provide a scientific explanation for how it's not vulgar. [quote]</span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Calibri\">It is \u201cscientific\u201d in the sense that the HAP will try to create a logical, reasonable and possible for the current \u201cscientific\u201d consensus, like \u201cOh a cat must have jumped on the car\u201d. No one would think \u201cOh, someone must be rubbing his magic ring\u201d. And that is good for technos and bad for mystical. Got it now?<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1543101-do-you-like-paradox?p=1544495#post1544495\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yes, to refute your statement that it would be difficult to do so.</div> </div> </div> </div></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Calibri\">Your first example is a completely different effect and your second one is still coincident. Also, this attempt to try and make the effect vulgar just proves how coincident it is and how \u201crandom\u201d (in quotes because we all know it isn\u2019t truly random) car alarms triggers.</span><br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Calibri\"><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1543101-do-you-like-paradox?p=1544495#post1544495\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Wow, you deleted a post and didn't bother editing the next post where you said, &quot;Yes, paradox is caused by consensus...&quot;<br /> <br /> Take your gaslighting BS and shove it.</div> </div> </div> </div></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Calibri\">I have not deleted nor edited any of my posts. You probably misread it. Can you show me the post with your quote? Because I NEVER said that. Any moderator could confirm that I am not lying.</span><br /> <br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Calibri\">Also I don\u2019t appreciate your tone. I got a warning for answering you (I hope you got one as well, since you started going aggressive), and I don\u2019t plan to get another, so I won\u2019t play your game of insults.</span><br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25411-travislegge\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar25411_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"25411\" data-vbnamecard=\"25411\">TravisLegge</a><span style=\"font-family:Calibri\">, could you step in and tell this gentleman that I have not deleted nor edited any post of mine? Also, he should watch his language.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1543101-do-you-like-paradox?p=1544495#post1544495\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">1) There's massive holes in your logic that never gets back to the whole &quot;obeying&quot; thing (and when you got back to that in previous posts you just played semantic games). Lets try something simple: Is driving 26 mph in an area with a 25 mph speed limit obeying traffic laws, or is it violating traffic laws even if by such a small degree that the odds of getting a ticket are negligible?</div> </div> </div> </div></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Calibri\">Driving at 26 mph in a area with 25 mph limit is not obeying traffic laws. Traffic laws, however are very well stablished, consensus is not. Just an observation.</span><br /> <br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Calibri\"><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1543101-do-you-like-paradox?p=1544495#post1544495\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">2) What causes Paradox is Awakened magic screwing with Reality. Vulgar magic increases the potential for local Reality to snap back to normal in a fashion harmful to the mage, but the 'snap back' is why magic that isn't vulgar can still generate Paradox, and why witnesses impact the potential snap back as well.</div> </div> </div> </div></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Calibri\">Are you talking about botches here?</span><br /> <br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Calibri\"><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1543101-do-you-like-paradox?p=1544495#post1544495\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">3) The only needless things are your overt lies.</div> </div> </div> </div></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Calibri\">Again, going aggressive. I wont fall for that again. Good luck with this kind of argument.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1543101-do-you-like-paradox?p=1544495#post1544495\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">No, you are because you don't like what happens if we don't constrain the discussion to your chosen criteria.<br /> <br /> The point started by a different poster, was that mystic mages don't feel like they have a real Focus when the game stresses coincidental magic so much because they have to act like technos to be coincidental. Your sidetracking about vulgar magic is, in fact, bullshit.<br /> <br /> The point of focusing on coincidental magic is that Focus still matters to mystic mages because they don't do techno style magic when doing coincidental magic. They still do mystic magic. This is the whole &quot;obey vs. subtle&quot; debate in a nutshell. Doing small subtle changes isn't turning a mystic into a techno, it's just being subtle enough people don't see what you're doing. Obeying would mean becoming a techno because you'd be doing things according to Consensus's rules, not taking advantage of Consensus's blind spots.<br /> <br /> Analysis of anything beyond that is a distraction.</div> </div> </div> </div></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Calibri\">Of course, in a debate about coincident magick, vulgarity will also be the subject as they are opposites. The same goes for mystics and technos. The user said that mystic mages have that focus issue with consensus, which implies that technos do not have it. And that is already a comparison.</span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Calibri\">So, let\u2019s try one more time, without insults and semantics discussions:</span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Calibri\">Your mage wants to levitate a coin that is on the ground to his hand.</span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Calibri\">If you are playing a technomancer, you could pull your Zero Point Energy Field Manipulator, point at the coin and guide it in the air to your hand. Cutting edge technology, aligned with the mage paradigm, and still possibly coincident.</span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Calibri\">Now, the mystic hermetic pulls his wand and waves at the coin, levitating it to his hand. That\u2019s aligned with his paradigm, but is vulgar magick. If he wants to make it in a coincident way, he will have to burn his brain out thinking on how to do it without violating consensus. The best he could do is to slide the coin to his feet and blame \u201cthe wind\u201d or some other excuse that is acceptable inside the *current scientific consensus*, otherwise it is going to be vulgar.</span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Calibri\">In this sense, the mystic has to \u201cdisguise\u201d his paradigm inside the consensus and often times that\u2019s not even possible. While the technomancer can bring his bs technology and accomplish a lot more.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1543101-do-you-like-paradox?p=1544495#post1544495\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Your biological age clearly doesn't stop you from trying to manipulating the conversation, lie, and other bullshit that has no clear motivation besides Internet pettiness. You could be 50, and it wouldn't stop you from acting like a particularly bratty 8 year old.</div> </div> </div> </div></span><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1543101-do-you-like-paradox?p=1544495#post1544495\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Calibri\">So, I'm right, your wrong, but your desire for Internet points is stopping you from just admitting it.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> Yes, I'm not the only lying to people on the Internet because I said something stupid on a forum about a game.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> I wish, it would make dealing with your crap easier.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> Then my point stands. You don't care about what the words actually mean, you only care about bending twisting them to make yourself &quot;right&quot; on the Internet.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> Wow, how mature, &quot;I'm going to take the high ground by insulting you too!&quot; When you catch me lying, try again, liar.</span></div> </div> </div> </div><span style=\"font-family:Calibri\">Wow, that was a nice combo of aggressive posting. Hahahahahaha. Very nice.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1543101-do-you-like-paradox?p=1544495#post1544495\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">And yet again, you contradict yourself. &quot;Flying under the radar&quot; *is* providing a scientific explanation...&quot; you can't keep your arguments straight, and instead of trying to get better arguments, you lie about it.</div> </div> </div> </div></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Calibri\">I will try to explain what I meant so you won\u2019t think I\u2019m lying:</span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Calibri\">For a HOP, there is no scientific explanation for why rubbing a ring would trigger a car alarm. HOP knows that nothing triggered the alarm, no cats jumping on it, no apple falling from the tree on top of it, nor any burglar trying to open the doors. It knows it was the mage and that is not a scientific explanation.</span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Calibri\">But HAP doesn\u2019t know any of that. He just saw that man with a ring on his hand and suddenly a car alarm starts screaming. This makes HAP create a \u201cscientific\u201d (in quotes, as in, consensus allowed) explanation. He will try to reason and think about all the explanations I gave above, or simply think \u201cdamn alarms always triggering for nothing\u201d. What will NOT pass through his mind would be \u201cThat man over there rubbed his ring and triggered the car alarm\u201d.</span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Calibri\">So, the HAP creates a consensus aligned explanation. But there are no REAL (HOP like) scientific explanation. I hope this is clear now.</span><br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1543101-do-you-like-paradox?p=1544495#post1544495\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><span style=\"font-family:Calibri\">Not really, because cars don't explode on a regular enough basis for people to consider a car just exploding to be normal. Like your grenade launcher quip, the &quot;1001&quot; ways are just not using magic, or using magic to do something they could have done without it. The work to make it coincidental is greater than the work to do it mundanely.</span></div> </div> </div> </div><span style=\"font-family:Calibri\">Fair enough, I provided another example above.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1543101-do-you-like-paradox?p=1544495#post1544495\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">No, the lying is bad faith.</div> </div> </div> </div></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Calibri\">Lying..Hahahahaha<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1543101-do-you-like-paradox?p=1544495#post1544495\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That presumes Reality is a thinking entity in Mage.<br /> <br /> When you get a cut, you don't just heal back with fresh skin. You get scabs, you risk infections and your body responds with inflammation, etc. The worse the cut, the more your body does beyond grow new skin to seal the cut.<br /> <br /> Horns are like a nasty scab. It's a big ass sign something wrong happened, that's part of the process of getting back to just skin.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> M20 leaves a lot of it up to the ST to decide for the tone of their own games, and because M20 was trying to remain appealing to multiple editions of the game which had their own peculiarities in this arena (1e/2e was much more &quot;punishment motivated&quot; Paradox, while Revised was more &quot;natural force of metaphysics&quot; Paradox).<br /></div> </div> </div> </div></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Calibri\">That is another issue I have with paradox. I like the \u201cnatural force of metaphysics\u201d paradox a lot better.</span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Calibri\">However, in our real life, nature is always very efficient, doing the least amount of work. And in M20 backlashes seem to do more in the direction of cutting instead of healing. Growing horns feels like you are trying to heal the cut with a knife, since the cut was made by a vulgar effect in the first place.</span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Calibri\">Wouldn\u2019t you agree that closing the wound would be turning the mage back to human (on the transmutation example), or doing whatever is the opposite the spell is doing and bringing reality to it\u2019s normal state? I understand that it would still need a scab, but shouldn\u2019t a scab in Reality be something that is possible inside consensus?</span><br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3153-lord-revan","name":"Lord Revan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3153_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1419"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}